1
00:01:22,508 --> 00:01:24,322
[Ominous music]

2
00:01:26,701 --> 00:01:28,055
Oh, my Lord...

3
00:01:28,056 --> 00:01:30,359
No, Lord!
I didn't steal it, Lord!

4
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:32,555
Yes, my Lord.
Thirty years old.

5
00:01:32,681 --> 00:01:35,248
He stole pepper from the warehouse.

6
00:01:35,249 --> 00:01:37,612
No, my Lord! No, my Lord...

7
00:01:37,741 --> 00:01:39,791
- Take him away!
- I didn't do it, my Lord!

8
00:01:39,792 --> 00:01:41,012
My Lord... My Lord...

9
00:01:41,013 --> 00:01:42,179
I didn't do it, Lord!

10
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,604
No, please!

11
00:01:44,417 --> 00:01:45,670
[Whip cracks]

12
00:01:46,264 --> 00:01:47,531
[Horse hooves]

13
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:49,975
[Horse neighs]

14
00:01:53,497 --> 00:01:57,123
[Beating, screams]

15
00:02:03,146 --> 00:02:04,633
[Melancholic background music]

16
00:02:07,657 --> 00:02:10,028
I am the new Collector,
Clement Manuel.

17
00:02:10,394 --> 00:02:12,487
An urgent message
has been sent directly

18
00:02:12,488 --> 00:02:14,428
by the Honourable British Resident,

19
00:02:14,429 --> 00:02:16,339
Sir Joseph William Richard,

20
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:20,116
to be conveyed to the honourable
Pattelar Kunjambu Nambiar.

21
00:02:21,589 --> 00:02:23,030
[Mysterious background music]

22
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:25,693
Sir, please try to understand.

23
00:02:25,994 --> 00:02:27,951
I am telling the truth.

24
00:02:27,952 --> 00:02:29,940
I have spoken to the company.

25
00:02:30,373 --> 00:02:31,465
[Scoffs]

26
00:02:31,466 --> 00:02:32,576
An ultimatum?

27
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:35,872
Sir?

28
00:02:36,036 --> 00:02:38,651
May I meet
Mr. Nambiar in person?

29
00:02:38,935 --> 00:02:39,942
Please?

30
00:02:41,398 --> 00:02:44,199
So, you want to meet
Pattelar Kunjambu Nambiar in person?

31
00:02:45,678 --> 00:02:47,031
[Laughs]

32
00:02:47,749 --> 00:02:50,300
Come to Talakaveri
for the Kaveri Sankramanam festival.

33
00:02:50,702 --> 00:02:52,445
As one among the thousands,
you can catch a glimpse of him.

34
00:02:52,446 --> 00:02:54,881
[Intense background music rises]

35
00:02:58,202 --> 00:03:00,754
The forest lands adjacent to
the Chandragiri River are now

36
00:03:00,755 --> 00:03:03,663
officially under
the company's protected zone.

37
00:03:06,154 --> 00:03:09,387
Since the transfer of the land to the
company has long since lapsed,

38
00:03:09,388 --> 00:03:14,507
you are hereby notified that your contract
stands cancelled with retrospective effect.

39
00:03:20,235 --> 00:03:21,235
Mr. Richard,

40
00:03:21,327 --> 00:03:25,293
consider this your final
and irrefutable warning.

41
00:03:25,294 --> 00:03:27,074
Or... Or else...

42
00:03:27,317 --> 00:03:29,043
[Gunshot]

43
00:03:29,742 --> 00:03:32,328
[Horse squeals]

44
00:03:32,729 --> 00:03:33,729
[Gunshot]

45
00:03:34,032 --> 00:03:35,412
[Elephant trumpets]

46
00:03:35,611 --> 00:03:36,772
[Horse neighs]

47
00:03:36,773 --> 00:03:37,818
[Galloping hooves]

48
00:03:37,819 --> 00:03:38,976
[Elephant trumpets]

49
00:03:38,977 --> 00:03:40,277
[Elephant trumpets loudly]

50
00:03:41,291 --> 00:03:42,471
[Head crushed]

51
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,235
[Screams]

52
00:03:44,236 --> 00:03:46,155
[Intense background music rises]

53
00:03:46,156 --> 00:03:47,887
[Woman] My son!

54
00:04:06,981 --> 00:04:09,114
[Chandragiri Forest, Thomapuram]

55
00:04:09,970 --> 00:04:12,110
[Drums beating]

56
00:04:13,714 --> 00:04:14,860
O Goddess!

57
00:04:14,861 --> 00:04:16,292
Mom, look!
It's Chachan.

58
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:21,343
My dear, fold your hands and pray.

59
00:04:21,983 --> 00:04:22,837
Dear goddess...

60
00:04:22,838 --> 00:04:24,795
Father Jerome had come
from Neeleshwaram.

61
00:04:24,796 --> 00:04:26,117
[Screams]

62
00:04:26,118 --> 00:04:27,124
- He left late.
- Father!

63
00:04:27,571 --> 00:04:30,377
- Has it been long since it started?
- It has only just begun, Father.

64
00:04:30,378 --> 00:04:31,404
Hello, my dear!

65
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:36,091
Look, it's Keluchachan as Bali!

66
00:04:41,121 --> 00:04:44,073
Iype from Chumathra is very unwell…

67
00:04:44,074 --> 00:04:45,456
Seems like it is Malaria.

68
00:04:45,457 --> 00:04:46,745
- Keluchacha!
- Yes!

69
00:04:46,746 --> 00:04:50,511
But why did Rama shoot
Bali from the shadows?

70
00:04:50,512 --> 00:04:51,560
Well, well!

71
00:04:51,561 --> 00:04:55,330
If they fought face-to-face, Rama
could never have defeated Bali.

72
00:04:55,552 --> 00:04:58,630
Why? Is Bali a greater god than Rama?

73
00:04:58,825 --> 00:05:01,572
No, Bali isn't a god.

74
00:05:01,712 --> 00:05:03,061
Just a monkey.

75
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,655
A monkey no bigger than a man.

76
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:07,973
Shall we head out then, Kelu?

77
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:09,765
- Let's go, Father…
- Come on, hurry up.

78
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,554
- So, shall we leave?
- Yeah…

79
00:05:12,911 --> 00:05:15,171
Father, hold my hand!

80
00:05:15,292 --> 00:05:16,551
There you go!

81
00:05:16,776 --> 00:05:20,504
Father, would our Jesus have
met the God Bali?

82
00:05:20,911 --> 00:05:24,620
- Tell me!
- Jesus, this kid is just too much!

83
00:05:24,621 --> 00:05:26,158
You have such strange questions!

84
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:28,686
[Sudden sound]
Oh no! My dear! Oh god!

85
00:05:28,687 --> 00:05:29,516
- Oh no!
- Mom!

86
00:05:29,517 --> 00:05:30,594
[Gunshot]

87
00:05:30,595 --> 00:05:32,074
- Keluchacha!
- Don't cry, dear. Don't cry.

88
00:05:32,075 --> 00:05:34,243
- Kelu?
- Paappi, hurry up!

89
00:05:34,599 --> 00:05:36,439
They are Pattelar's goons.
Come quickly!

90
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,968
If they spot us,
they will finish us!

91
00:05:37,969 --> 00:05:41,980
I came here scared for my life,
abandoning the land I bought in Rajapuram.

92
00:05:41,981 --> 00:05:44,716
And these scoundrels won't
let us be in peace even here!

93
00:05:46,931 --> 00:05:48,470
[Ropes creak under tension]

94
00:05:51,341 --> 00:05:52,654
[Thunder rumbles]

95
00:05:53,012 --> 00:05:54,012
Lord Jesus!

96
00:05:54,645 --> 00:05:56,276
What is this!!

97
00:05:56,911 --> 00:05:57,911
Jesus!

98
00:05:58,838 --> 00:06:00,237
Oh no!

99
00:06:00,238 --> 00:06:02,065
- My lord...
- Mom!

100
00:06:02,731 --> 00:06:04,131
O Lord of Israel!

101
00:06:04,831 --> 00:06:06,551
My lord!

102
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:08,767
What wrong did they do, Jesus!!

103
00:06:08,889 --> 00:06:10,663
[Baby crying]

104
00:06:12,952 --> 00:06:16,040
[Baby crying]
Sounds like a baby is crying.

105
00:06:16,273 --> 00:06:18,555
Yes, it's a baby crying.

106
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:22,327
- Kelu, look!
- That's right.

107
00:06:23,351 --> 00:06:25,340
- [Baby continues crying]
- It's a baby crying.

108
00:06:30,653 --> 00:06:32,706
Mom, look.

109
00:06:34,408 --> 00:06:37,008
[Baby crying]

110
00:06:37,821 --> 00:06:39,394
[Gentle music]

111
00:06:43,096 --> 00:06:45,770
[Baby continues crying]

112
00:06:50,791 --> 00:06:53,238
[Hopeful background music]

113
00:06:57,261 --> 00:06:59,014
[Knot comes undone]

114
00:07:00,741 --> 00:07:01,881
Dear lord!

115
00:07:12,761 --> 00:07:14,041
O Father in Heaven!

116
00:07:23,926 --> 00:07:26,199
[Background music swells]

117
00:07:31,768 --> 00:07:33,061
Little one!

118
00:07:36,695 --> 00:07:38,488
[Majestic background music rises]

119
00:07:52,937 --> 00:07:57,139
THE CHURCH ROWDY

120
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:17,470
Does the land upon which we live today

121
00:08:18,215 --> 00:08:20,799
truly belong to us?

122
00:08:25,071 --> 00:08:29,595
This land, which has passed through
countless hands across countless ages…

123
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:31,653
Who are its rightful heirs?

124
00:08:35,047 --> 00:08:37,471
Through invasion and dominion,

125
00:08:38,513 --> 00:08:40,540
by trespass and
taking possession,

126
00:08:41,051 --> 00:08:43,739
we have claimed
ownership of this land…

127
00:08:44,530 --> 00:08:47,004
Will it still remain ours tomorrow?

128
00:08:49,348 --> 00:08:52,997
The battle for land did
not begin today or yesterday.

129
00:08:53,974 --> 00:08:56,568
Nor shall it end
in the tomorrows yet to come.

130
00:08:56,569 --> 00:08:57,999
[Kunnumpuram]

131
00:09:02,559 --> 00:09:04,294
[Kurushumala Hill]

132
00:09:18,546 --> 00:09:20,132
[Amaravati river]

133
00:09:23,648 --> 00:09:25,249
[Kaaniyaar]

134
00:09:30,785 --> 00:09:34,005
On April 5, 1957,

135
00:09:34,436 --> 00:09:35,962
through a general election,

136
00:09:36,301 --> 00:09:37,603
for the first time in the world,

137
00:09:37,912 --> 00:09:40,516
a Communist government
assumed power,

138
00:09:41,242 --> 00:09:42,339
right here, in Kerala.

139
00:09:45,856 --> 00:09:49,182
Against the land reforms
implemented by that government,

140
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,507
in the struggle for land,

141
00:09:51,998 --> 00:09:54,933
various caste and religious
organisations across Kerala

142
00:09:55,318 --> 00:09:57,588
took to the streets to protest

143
00:09:57,589 --> 00:09:59,258
against the Communist government.

144
00:10:00,050 --> 00:10:01,464
The Liberation Struggle.

145
00:10:05,027 --> 00:10:06,399
[Telephone rings]

146
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,527
[E.N.S., Chief Minister]

147
00:10:09,163 --> 00:10:12,863
The government resolved
to counter the protest.

148
00:10:13,509 --> 00:10:14,795
This is that file.

149
00:10:16,473 --> 00:10:19,260
But the Communist
Chief Minister did not know that...

150
00:10:19,612 --> 00:10:20,774
Tell them to leave!

151
00:10:20,775 --> 00:10:21,855
[Pen scratching on paper]

152
00:10:22,035 --> 00:10:26,864
...a small village in the eastern
hills was ready to turn into a tempest

153
00:10:27,470 --> 00:10:32,544
with the deadly power to
uproot his government.

154
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,372
Kaaniyaar!

155
00:10:34,373 --> 00:10:35,406
[1958 - Kaaniyaar]

156
00:10:35,407 --> 00:10:37,098
[Background music intensifies]

157
00:10:37,634 --> 00:10:39,234
O Almighty Lord!

158
00:10:39,798 --> 00:10:42,961
From the malevolent forces
that defy the sacred laws,

159
00:10:43,218 --> 00:10:46,068
guard thy people diligently.

160
00:10:46,693 --> 00:10:48,385
Those who blaspheme against God,

161
00:10:48,603 --> 00:10:50,567
those who burn our sanctuaries,

162
00:10:50,759 --> 00:10:52,605
those who have slaughtered the faithful.

163
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,550
They have now set foot
upon our very soil.

164
00:10:55,551 --> 00:10:59,106
[Radio] Our district bureau reports
that the Liberation Struggle,

165
00:10:59,459 --> 00:11:04,231
formed against the policies of the State
Government is spreading to more locations.

166
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:06,950
- In Alappuzha--
[Slogans]

167
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:09,592
Under the pretext of
the Land Reform Act,

168
00:11:10,092 --> 00:11:12,242
they will seize our lands,

169
00:11:12,585 --> 00:11:15,659
and soon plant red flags
upon our altars!

170
00:11:15,793 --> 00:11:18,167
Long live the revolution!

171
00:11:18,473 --> 00:11:20,689
They will shatter our sacred idols!

172
00:11:21,008 --> 00:11:22,843
They will lead our children astray

173
00:11:23,248 --> 00:11:25,181
and into the clutches of Satan!

174
00:11:28,642 --> 00:11:29,686
- Outha...
- Yeah?

175
00:11:29,687 --> 00:11:31,119
What the hell is this thuggery?

176
00:11:31,284 --> 00:11:33,383
Is the church gate
the place for their revolution?

177
00:11:33,384 --> 00:11:35,231
Kuriachan!
This is their handiwork.

178
00:11:39,915 --> 00:11:40,916
Stick it back!

179
00:11:42,366 --> 00:11:43,366
Fast!

180
00:11:44,777 --> 00:11:46,423
[Background music intensifies]

181
00:11:46,761 --> 00:11:50,239
I repeat to you
the words of Holy Pope Pius XI

182
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,799
a hundred thousand times over.

183
00:11:53,542 --> 00:11:57,369
I utter those words
from the graves of the holy churches

184
00:11:57,370 --> 00:12:02,226
that were razed to the ground
in Albania and the Soviet Union!

185
00:12:03,981 --> 00:12:06,622
Communism is the enemy of God.

186
00:12:07,006 --> 00:12:09,633
Communism is the enemy of God!

187
00:12:10,150 --> 00:12:11,411
[Thunder rumbles]

188
00:12:11,497 --> 00:12:13,044
[Background music roars]

189
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,867
Behold, he comes…

190
00:12:18,914 --> 00:12:20,724
The coming of the Antichrist!

191
00:12:21,285 --> 00:12:22,957
[Background music crescendos]

192
00:12:22,958 --> 00:12:23,958
[Thunder]

193
00:12:26,661 --> 00:12:28,464
Now we have to fear
the communists too!

194
00:12:29,119 --> 00:12:30,984
Son, where's Johnny?

195
00:12:31,399 --> 00:12:32,702
Where's Johnny?

196
00:12:33,799 --> 00:12:34,830
Johnny!

197
00:12:34,831 --> 00:12:35,838
- Johnny?
- Johnny?

198
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:37,787
- Johnny?
- Dad!

199
00:12:38,021 --> 00:12:39,021
Johnny!

200
00:12:39,339 --> 00:12:40,360
Johnny?

201
00:12:40,997 --> 00:12:42,910
Oh God! Where did he go?

202
00:12:42,911 --> 00:12:44,911
- Johnny!
- Johnny?

203
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,853
Johnnyboy!

204
00:12:48,577 --> 00:12:49,587
Hey!

205
00:12:49,714 --> 00:12:50,864
[Thunder rumbles]

206
00:12:50,865 --> 00:12:53,337
Chettayi, look!
A comet over that mountain.

207
00:12:56,731 --> 00:12:58,134
That's Thariyottumala Hill.

208
00:12:58,411 --> 00:12:59,990
That's the land of demons.

209
00:13:00,371 --> 00:13:03,400
How many times have I told you
not even to look there?

210
00:13:03,719 --> 00:13:04,871
Come on, keep moving.

211
00:13:08,267 --> 00:13:09,645
[Thunder rumbles]

212
00:13:10,402 --> 00:13:12,155
[Menacing background music roars]

213
00:13:19,467 --> 00:13:22,156
Paappi, there's a fight happening
at the market. Come fast!

214
00:13:22,157 --> 00:13:23,303
[Kaaniyaar]

215
00:13:24,188 --> 00:13:25,214
Outha, get down.

216
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:26,765
[Loud pounding]

217
00:13:27,951 --> 00:13:29,391
[Laughs loudly]

218
00:13:30,187 --> 00:13:32,299
[Background music intensifies]

219
00:13:41,525 --> 00:13:42,885
Oh God! Matthayi Chetta...

220
00:13:42,886 --> 00:13:44,289
- What happened, brother?
- Dear Lord!

221
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,112
George, please stop!

222
00:13:47,198 --> 00:13:48,260
You'll kill them.

223
00:13:48,513 --> 00:13:49,898
Don't anyone dare say a word!

224
00:13:50,103 --> 00:13:52,746
Who gave the order to put a padlock
and lock up George's shop?

225
00:13:52,917 --> 00:13:53,924
Who was it?!

226
00:13:54,577 --> 00:13:56,658
These guys are taking
the beating meant for you.

227
00:13:56,756 --> 00:13:58,750
Just stay silent,
draw a cross and watch!

228
00:13:59,095 --> 00:14:00,454
Oh no!
Father, look at this!

229
00:14:00,455 --> 00:14:02,360
You've got quite some nerve!

230
00:14:02,615 --> 00:14:04,719
Hey! Hey, George!

231
00:14:05,095 --> 00:14:06,101
My son...

232
00:14:06,457 --> 00:14:09,440
When the Communists came
asking for this shop,

233
00:14:09,441 --> 00:14:11,021
which is our church property,

234
00:14:11,459 --> 00:14:14,335
I locked it up, to stop
them from occupying it.

235
00:14:15,283 --> 00:14:16,314
Here,

236
00:14:16,315 --> 00:14:17,991
you keep the key now.

237
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,375
- Right, Outha?
- Yes.

238
00:14:19,376 --> 00:14:20,383
Yeah.

239
00:14:20,686 --> 00:14:21,958
Listen, George...

240
00:14:22,449 --> 00:14:25,420
with Communist demons surrounding us,

241
00:14:25,421 --> 00:14:27,887
we, the parish, must stand united

242
00:14:27,888 --> 00:14:29,752
and face them together.

243
00:14:29,903 --> 00:14:31,966
- Is that so?
- "Is that so," you ask?

244
00:14:32,611 --> 00:14:34,869
Even on Kurishumala Hill, where we
planned to build our church,

245
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:37,165
those fellows have gone
and planted their red flag.

246
00:14:37,581 --> 00:14:39,946
That cursed red flag!

247
00:14:41,136 --> 00:14:44,622
It's a flag that defies every
Christian value we hold dear.

248
00:14:46,024 --> 00:14:47,380
Alright, you may all leave now.

249
00:14:47,381 --> 00:14:48,535
Go on, get moving.

250
00:14:48,536 --> 00:14:50,136
Didn't you hear Father?
Everyone, out!

251
00:14:50,137 --> 00:14:51,144
Pathrose, come here.

252
00:14:51,255 --> 00:14:53,084
- Everyone, move along.
- George, my son...

253
00:14:53,414 --> 00:14:54,608
Come to the parsonage.

254
00:14:54,609 --> 00:14:57,310
- I need to tell you something important.
- Come, everyone follow me.

255
00:14:58,044 --> 00:14:59,084
Don't forget!

256
00:14:59,894 --> 00:15:00,987
Paappi, come on!

257
00:15:08,266 --> 00:15:09,269
Outha, look!

258
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:10,547
Father!

259
00:15:16,455 --> 00:15:18,402
To all of you who lack the
decency to keep your word...

260
00:15:18,403 --> 00:15:20,474
If this red flag is what's
keeping you awake at night,

261
00:15:22,001 --> 00:15:24,067
then from today,
George is a Communist too!

262
00:15:26,774 --> 00:15:27,781
And listen...

263
00:15:28,419 --> 00:15:29,872
this flag stays right here,

264
00:15:30,568 --> 00:15:32,681
right under the Saint's nose!

265
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:34,540
[Tense background music]

266
00:15:35,953 --> 00:15:37,816
I'm telling all you low-lives...

267
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:41,919
This is the flag blessed and
planted by Quintal George!

268
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:46,216
In the name of the church
and the priest, if anyone touches this,

269
00:15:46,387 --> 00:15:48,161
I'll chop off the hand
that touches it,

270
00:15:48,162 --> 00:15:49,571
and the one that let it!

271
00:15:58,246 --> 00:16:00,905
I am the son of Yona Mappila,
the man the Communists slaughtered

272
00:16:00,906 --> 00:16:02,356
for donating
land to this church!

273
00:16:02,357 --> 00:16:04,799
I want to see today whether
my word holds any weight or not.

274
00:16:05,248 --> 00:16:07,396
Weren't you trying to
groom Quintal George

275
00:16:07,397 --> 00:16:10,044
to be the saviour of
Kunnumpuram Church, Father?

276
00:16:10,349 --> 00:16:13,364
Now he's a Communist too.
Serves you right!

277
00:16:13,365 --> 00:16:15,761
Father, there's no point in
just talking like this anymore.

278
00:16:16,004 --> 00:16:18,658
Find a way to follow the instructions
from the Church's circular.

279
00:16:18,659 --> 00:16:20,536
Today it's Quintal,
but who knows how many

280
00:16:20,664 --> 00:16:22,989
will follow him and
the red flag tomorrow?

281
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:24,483
Don't say I didn't warn you.

282
00:16:24,588 --> 00:16:25,588
Yes!

283
00:16:28,334 --> 00:16:30,515
[Rain falls]

284
00:16:30,516 --> 00:16:33,294
I'm sure you've all heard that
we've received the Church circular.

285
00:16:33,295 --> 00:16:35,266
To counter the Communist menace,

286
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:37,625
the Church has decided to form

287
00:16:37,626 --> 00:16:40,787
a defence force in every parish.

288
00:16:42,390 --> 00:16:43,863
The Christopher Force.

289
00:16:44,229 --> 00:16:45,976
[Powerful background music intensifies]

290
00:16:47,902 --> 00:16:51,746
By giving physical training to the
youth of our parish,

291
00:16:51,747 --> 00:16:54,295
we will form our own army.

292
00:16:54,501 --> 00:16:56,440
From Kozhikode and Nilambur,

293
00:16:56,441 --> 00:16:59,689
bringing Kalari masters
and veteran soldiers,

294
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:02,879
training has already begun
in Changanassery and Pala.

295
00:17:04,701 --> 00:17:06,010
What I'm saying is that...

296
00:17:06,134 --> 00:17:09,924
They have been trying to lure our people
into joining their party...

297
00:17:10,082 --> 00:17:11,902
And now, Quintal George
has also joined them

298
00:17:11,903 --> 00:17:13,386
to lead their way.

299
00:17:13,708 --> 00:17:15,729
So, at the earliest,

300
00:17:15,730 --> 00:17:20,104
we must find the toughest
brawler in all of Kerala.

301
00:17:20,742 --> 00:17:23,009
A warrior with the grit
and power to drive

302
00:17:23,010 --> 00:17:26,797
those Antiochians and
their pawns across the sea.

303
00:17:28,057 --> 00:17:30,595
No matter the cost,
we must bring him here

304
00:17:30,596 --> 00:17:33,381
and crown him the 'Christopher'
of Kunnumpuram Church.

305
00:17:33,688 --> 00:17:35,541
But Father, how can we
find such a man now?

306
00:17:35,704 --> 00:17:37,197
Shouldn't we find
the right person?

307
00:17:37,322 --> 00:17:39,801
That's why the young priest
and the trustee have gone north.

308
00:17:40,136 --> 00:17:41,594
I am certain,

309
00:17:42,730 --> 00:17:44,426
the Lord will show us a way.

310
00:17:44,889 --> 00:17:46,876
[Powerful background music intensifies]

311
00:18:04,499 --> 00:18:06,168
Did you find him?
Did you find the rowdy?

312
00:18:06,288 --> 00:18:08,895
- That's exactly where we're heading.
- So we haven't reached?

313
00:18:08,896 --> 00:18:10,293
We've just reached Thommapuram.

314
00:18:10,294 --> 00:18:13,015
That's what I've been saying.

315
00:18:13,925 --> 00:18:18,373
We're on our way to meet
the rowdy, aren't we?

316
00:18:18,374 --> 00:18:21,679
Father, it's not enough if we
find some random rowdy.

317
00:18:22,337 --> 00:18:23,732
He should be a faithful Christian.

318
00:18:24,001 --> 00:18:26,583
- Let's meet the man first, Devassy.
- Yeah.

319
00:18:26,823 --> 00:18:29,523
Well, well! Look who's here.

320
00:18:29,824 --> 00:18:31,999
Paramashivan and Mandodari.

321
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,056
Ah, Father...

322
00:18:33,057 --> 00:18:34,958
Hey, where is Ravanan?

323
00:18:34,959 --> 00:18:37,631
He's headed into the forest, Father.

324
00:18:37,632 --> 00:18:39,011
Oh, man...

325
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:40,805
What a pity!

326
00:18:40,806 --> 00:18:42,076
Are they Folk Drama artists?

327
00:18:42,536 --> 00:18:44,098
We got a little delayed.

328
00:18:44,379 --> 00:18:48,091
Otherwise, we could've watched the Ravana
Charitham play to our heart's content

329
00:18:48,092 --> 00:18:49,674
before returning.

330
00:18:49,845 --> 00:18:51,051
What a pity.

331
00:18:51,052 --> 00:18:53,103
- Are we going to watch a play?
- Monayi, turn the vehicle.

332
00:18:53,104 --> 00:18:54,744
Ask him about the rowdy, Father.

333
00:18:54,745 --> 00:18:57,137
Father, weren't we just
talking about that rowdy?

334
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:58,584
That's right.

335
00:18:58,872 --> 00:19:01,452
That's exactly what I was saying.

336
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:04,393
To finish narrating his story,

337
00:19:04,498 --> 00:19:06,458
it'll take all night.

338
00:19:08,066 --> 00:19:11,608
The fierce Ravana,
the Lord of Lanka!

339
00:19:11,609 --> 00:19:13,701
[Heartwarming music begins]

340
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,903
131,

341
00:19:16,299 --> 00:19:18,139
132...

342
00:19:18,758 --> 00:19:20,404
[Playful background music]

343
00:19:21,481 --> 00:19:25,277
134, 135...

344
00:19:25,278 --> 00:19:26,310
136...

345
00:19:26,311 --> 00:19:29,062
Aashaan is going for 300 today.

346
00:19:29,550 --> 00:19:31,764
[Heartwarming music swells]

347
00:19:35,401 --> 00:19:36,634
[Laughs loudly]

348
00:19:36,635 --> 00:19:37,944
- Did he surface?
- Sali...

349
00:19:37,945 --> 00:19:39,358
- What's the count?
- Aashaan!

350
00:19:39,585 --> 00:19:41,138
What was the count?
Two hundred and...?

351
00:19:41,139 --> 00:19:42,505
140!

352
00:19:43,045 --> 00:19:44,314
Huh?! 140?

353
00:19:44,315 --> 00:19:46,122
I counted up to 200
while I was underwater!

354
00:19:46,123 --> 00:19:47,976
It's only reached 140!

355
00:19:47,977 --> 00:19:49,176
Sali! Tell them!

356
00:19:49,496 --> 00:19:51,123
- No, no!
- Yeah, yeah... it's 200.

357
00:19:51,304 --> 00:19:52,588
Get lost... it's 200.

358
00:19:52,589 --> 00:19:53,767
Don't you dare lie to me!

359
00:19:53,768 --> 00:19:54,963
No, it's 140!

360
00:19:54,964 --> 00:19:56,748
You guys go to school
and learn to count first.

361
00:19:56,749 --> 00:19:58,366
It's only 140.

362
00:19:58,367 --> 00:20:00,603
Kids, don't start lying
at such a young age.

363
00:20:00,604 --> 00:20:02,168
- Hey!
- Who's that?

364
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,411
- Father!
- Oh wow!

365
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:06,491
I told you to come to the church office,

366
00:20:06,492 --> 00:20:08,107
and you're busy taking a dip here?

367
00:20:08,108 --> 00:20:10,292
I was just about to
head there after my bath.

368
00:20:10,293 --> 00:20:11,606
That's when these
kids showed up and...

369
00:20:11,607 --> 00:20:13,289
They wouldn't let me get out!
Right?

370
00:20:13,617 --> 00:20:16,471
Father, he's lying to you!

371
00:20:18,369 --> 00:20:20,135
This is our rowdy!

372
00:20:20,511 --> 00:20:21,572
Krishna Pillai.

373
00:20:21,730 --> 00:20:22,730
How is he?

374
00:20:22,943 --> 00:20:24,227
Shocked, aren't you?

375
00:20:24,902 --> 00:20:26,735
Oh, wonderful!
So he's not a Christian?

376
00:20:27,751 --> 00:20:31,903
I rushed out without even changing my
clothes, trusting this priest's word.

377
00:20:31,904 --> 00:20:33,499
It was all for nothing, Father!

378
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:37,523
This guy who spends his time playing
silly games with these children...

379
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:39,438
Is he going to drive
the Communists away?

380
00:20:39,557 --> 00:20:40,763
This nincompoop...

381
00:20:40,947 --> 00:20:43,969
can he even withstand a single blow
from Quintal George?

382
00:20:44,569 --> 00:20:46,424
And on top of that,
his name is Krishna Pillai!

383
00:20:46,936 --> 00:20:48,546
My dear Devassy, please calm down.

384
00:20:49,096 --> 00:20:52,246
We searched everywhere for Christopher
before we finally found him.

385
00:20:52,377 --> 00:20:55,344
All the other rowdies have already been
snapped up by the other churches.

386
00:20:56,311 --> 00:20:57,796
This is all that remains to us now.

387
00:20:58,311 --> 00:20:59,417
O Jesus!

388
00:21:00,144 --> 00:21:02,302
Father, I am not stepping
outside this town!

389
00:21:02,303 --> 00:21:04,331
- That is for certain!
- You, come here!

390
00:21:05,121 --> 00:21:07,839
Listen, that land stands
in need of this.

391
00:21:08,286 --> 00:21:09,784
God will bless you

392
00:21:10,166 --> 00:21:11,682
for doing this one thing.

393
00:21:11,683 --> 00:21:13,522
- Yeah, right.
- Not just that...

394
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:16,575
if you want to taste
real fish curry,

395
00:21:16,729 --> 00:21:20,688
you must try what the Christian
girls of Kaaniyaar make.

396
00:21:20,689 --> 00:21:22,876
Oh, please! As if fish curry
is something I've never had!

397
00:21:22,877 --> 00:21:23,926
Give it a rest, Father!

398
00:21:24,107 --> 00:21:25,114
My son,

399
00:21:25,757 --> 00:21:29,543
do you know the meaning
of the name 'Christopher'?

400
00:21:31,461 --> 00:21:33,541
He who bears Christ.

401
00:21:34,215 --> 00:21:37,652
When the portraits of the Christophers,
the guardians of the Church,

402
00:21:37,653 --> 00:21:40,201
are hung upon the Church walls tomorrow,

403
00:21:40,568 --> 00:21:42,229
you shall be among them!

404
00:21:42,842 --> 00:21:46,489
Tomorrow, you shall
become a part of history!

405
00:21:47,285 --> 00:21:48,912
[Background music intensifies]

406
00:21:49,695 --> 00:21:50,960
Hey, liar!

407
00:21:50,961 --> 00:21:52,722
- Just take them away!
- What did I even do?

408
00:21:53,872 --> 00:21:56,331
Father, does the Church really
need to get involved in this?

409
00:21:56,332 --> 00:21:57,847
Shouldn't the Church be
walking the path of peace?

410
00:21:57,848 --> 00:21:58,878
Hey, hey, hey...

411
00:21:58,879 --> 00:22:01,644
Don't you dare lecture
the Church on peace!

412
00:22:01,645 --> 00:22:05,172
We'll pay you 225 Rupees
per month instead of 200.

413
00:22:05,173 --> 00:22:07,647
That's final.
No more bargaining!

414
00:22:08,365 --> 00:22:09,793
Give him your hand!

415
00:22:10,165 --> 00:22:11,165
Shake on it!

416
00:22:11,506 --> 00:22:12,738
Forget the monthly rates!

417
00:22:12,832 --> 00:22:14,493
I'll return as soon
as the work is done!

418
00:22:14,494 --> 00:22:17,304
Fine! Come back immediately!
Right, Devassy?

419
00:22:18,018 --> 00:22:20,984
Why do you look so unhappy, Devassy?

420
00:22:21,285 --> 00:22:24,508
Well Father, if his name was

421
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:27,517
Avaran or Paily instead...

422
00:22:27,699 --> 00:22:30,647
the parishioners back home
would've been thrilled.

423
00:22:30,805 --> 00:22:32,033
Is that all?

424
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:35,352
If anyone asks your name there,

425
00:22:35,797 --> 00:22:37,247
tell them it's Pothan!

426
00:22:37,248 --> 00:22:38,383
- Pothan.
- Yes!

427
00:22:38,997 --> 00:22:40,296
Pothan Christopher!

428
00:22:40,297 --> 00:22:42,269
Why?
No way, Father!

429
00:22:42,270 --> 00:22:45,271
- Hey! Hey!
- Yeah, right! Pothan, huh?

430
00:22:45,569 --> 00:22:47,027
No way! Impossible!

431
00:22:50,506 --> 00:22:51,709
[Bus engine sound]

432
00:22:57,204 --> 00:22:58,824
[Snoring]

433
00:22:59,887 --> 00:23:00,891
Father!

434
00:23:01,580 --> 00:23:03,856
Who is this scumbag
sleeping over there, Father?

435
00:23:03,857 --> 00:23:04,964
Err... Well...

436
00:23:04,965 --> 00:23:06,811
We don't have place to sit.
And look at him!

437
00:23:06,812 --> 00:23:08,296
You look even prettier today.

438
00:23:08,297 --> 00:23:09,362
[Oxen lowing]

439
00:23:09,363 --> 00:23:11,045
[Brakes screech,
bus skids]

440
00:23:11,046 --> 00:23:12,516
[Screams,
people fall]

441
00:23:12,914 --> 00:23:15,655
- Aashaan. Aashaan, get up.
- Is that how you slam the brake?

442
00:23:15,656 --> 00:23:17,187
Drive the god damn thing right!

443
00:23:17,188 --> 00:23:18,188
Yeah!

444
00:23:19,182 --> 00:23:20,687
Then why don't you come and drive?!

445
00:23:21,612 --> 00:23:24,148
These are the hands that steer.
Don't make me use them on you.

446
00:23:24,149 --> 00:23:25,940
- I'll show this guy...
- Aashaan, let it go.

447
00:23:26,062 --> 00:23:27,715
We're in another town.
It'll be trouble.

448
00:23:27,716 --> 00:23:29,685
- What kind of trouble?
- Can you even drive a bus?

449
00:23:30,258 --> 00:23:31,959
- Um, no, I don't.
- Yeah, that's my point.

450
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,659
Hey, Rowdy!
Go question him!

451
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,418
Chettayi, tell him to drive properly.

452
00:23:36,419 --> 00:23:38,771
- What if something had happened to us?
- Yeah, that's right!

453
00:23:38,772 --> 00:23:41,127
Oh, you're hurt.
Oh no, my dear!

454
00:23:42,872 --> 00:23:44,300
- What happened?
- Dear!

455
00:23:44,301 --> 00:23:45,670
She's bleeding!

456
00:23:45,671 --> 00:23:48,303
- Seeing blood makes me uneasy.
- Aashaan is afraid of blood.

457
00:23:48,304 --> 00:23:49,604
Is there a hospital nearby?

458
00:23:49,605 --> 00:23:51,923
Father, he's scared of blood.

459
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,626
- Quiet, Devassy. Someone will hear.
- Hey! Hurry up, will you?

460
00:23:54,627 --> 00:23:56,016
What??

461
00:23:56,017 --> 00:23:59,006
I mean... Chetta, the girl's head
got bruised, and she's bleeding.

462
00:23:59,007 --> 00:24:00,120
Please, just go faster.

463
00:24:00,428 --> 00:24:01,594
[Loud gear shift]

464
00:24:02,427 --> 00:24:03,434
Seetha, my dear...

465
00:24:03,725 --> 00:24:06,092
[Emotional background music begins]

466
00:24:06,901 --> 00:24:08,087
Little one!

467
00:24:08,726 --> 00:24:10,093
My baby!

468
00:24:11,979 --> 00:24:13,159
[Woman crying]

469
00:24:14,489 --> 00:24:15,768
Seethamma!

470
00:24:17,321 --> 00:24:18,321
Hey!

471
00:24:21,116 --> 00:24:22,359
Seetha, my dear.

472
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:24,812
[Girl laughs]

473
00:24:25,551 --> 00:24:27,618
[Emotional music continues]

474
00:24:31,568 --> 00:24:33,215
[Woman continues crying]

475
00:24:34,295 --> 00:24:35,679
[Bus horn]

476
00:24:36,561 --> 00:24:37,993
[Bus bell rings]

477
00:24:39,603 --> 00:24:40,889
Chechi, I'll hold the child.

478
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:42,507
Don't be afraid.

479
00:24:44,848 --> 00:24:46,061
[Woman continues crying]

480
00:24:46,335 --> 00:24:48,674
- Where's the physician's clinic?
- It is over there.

481
00:24:48,675 --> 00:24:49,769
Oh, my god...

482
00:24:49,770 --> 00:24:50,789
Move!

483
00:24:51,188 --> 00:24:52,414
She'll be okay, Chechi.

484
00:24:52,811 --> 00:24:53,811
Physician!

485
00:24:57,637 --> 00:24:59,356
Aashaan!
Anything wrong?

486
00:24:59,553 --> 00:25:01,090
No, man.
Let me ask him.

487
00:25:03,363 --> 00:25:05,583
Doctor, is the wound on the
eyebrow pressure point?

488
00:25:06,418 --> 00:25:07,424
Huh?

489
00:25:08,736 --> 00:25:09,856
[Woman gasps]

490
00:25:10,404 --> 00:25:11,523
Don't worry.

491
00:25:12,659 --> 00:25:13,922
It's not on a pressure point.

492
00:25:14,192 --> 00:25:15,199
Phew!

493
00:25:15,687 --> 00:25:16,950
What a relief.

494
00:25:16,951 --> 00:25:17,958
Chechi, see?
I told you.

495
00:25:19,492 --> 00:25:20,498
Who are you?

496
00:25:23,877 --> 00:25:24,884
I've come from a bit far!

497
00:25:24,983 --> 00:25:26,630
Saali!
Oh, wow!

498
00:25:27,326 --> 00:25:29,811
Don't worry, the child is alright.
It's just a small wound.

499
00:25:29,812 --> 00:25:31,299
- Go on, go on.
- Come, dear.

500
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,659
- Saali...
- Yeah.

501
00:25:36,084 --> 00:25:38,715
This Kaaniyaar is like a mini Mangalore.

502
00:25:39,018 --> 00:25:40,318
- Huh?
- Yeah.

503
00:25:42,559 --> 00:25:43,970
"Damien's Paradise Casket."

504
00:25:44,172 --> 00:25:46,750
- Who's Damien? Is he the owner?
- No, he's a saint.

505
00:25:46,751 --> 00:25:47,858
Oh...

506
00:25:48,917 --> 00:25:50,837
Anyway, 'Paradise Casket'...
That's cool.

507
00:25:51,256 --> 00:25:53,002
- Back home, we call it a coffin.
- Oh.

508
00:25:53,399 --> 00:25:54,750
See that, Sali?

509
00:25:54,751 --> 00:25:57,549
To show respect to the dead,
now that's a big deal.

510
00:25:57,550 --> 00:26:00,773
- Yeah, of course! Of course!
- It shows the heart of Kaaniyaar's people.

511
00:26:00,774 --> 00:26:03,439
Oh! He's here?
Devassy!! Father!

512
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:05,135
Father, this is the guy.

513
00:26:05,431 --> 00:26:06,966
What are you guys doing?

514
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:08,769
Is this something that
should be kept hidden?

515
00:26:09,390 --> 00:26:12,707
- What's your name?
- Christopher. Pothan Christopher.

516
00:26:12,708 --> 00:26:15,117
Christopher?
Oh dear, oh dear...

517
00:26:15,118 --> 00:26:17,042
"Christopher" is in his name itself!

518
00:26:17,386 --> 00:26:18,513
Christopher!

519
00:26:18,774 --> 00:26:20,954
Look, didn't any of you recognise him?

520
00:26:21,119 --> 00:26:23,027
This is our "Christopher."

521
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:26,329
Kaaniyaar Sacred Heart
Church's Christopher.

522
00:26:27,364 --> 00:26:29,718
Son, come on!
Just come, will you?

523
00:26:30,178 --> 00:26:33,368
- Do you like the place?
- Yes, Father. It's a nice place.

524
00:26:33,369 --> 00:26:34,376
Well, this is nothing.

525
00:26:34,377 --> 00:26:36,877
Across the Amaravathi River,
lies Kunnumpuram.

526
00:26:37,158 --> 00:26:38,684
It is inhabited entirely by settlers.

527
00:26:39,043 --> 00:26:40,790
Beyond it stands Thariyottumala mountain.

528
00:26:40,791 --> 00:26:43,057
To the locals of Kunnumpuram,
it is the Devil's Mountain.

529
00:26:43,922 --> 00:26:46,042
And that's our Kaaniyaar's very own church.

530
00:26:46,138 --> 00:26:48,331
People also call it
the Kunnumpuram church.

531
00:26:48,778 --> 00:26:51,024
- They're the tribals of Kunnumpuram.
- Father!

532
00:26:53,375 --> 00:26:56,475
Kurishumala Hill is the very
soul of this land.

533
00:26:57,500 --> 00:27:01,296
We had in fact chosen that
site to build the new church.

534
00:27:01,297 --> 00:27:04,762
But those damn communists
planted a red flag there as well.

535
00:27:06,313 --> 00:27:07,889
And see what has come of it!

536
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:10,879
Only when all this is gone from Kaaniyaar

537
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,755
can we stand tall
with our heads held high!

538
00:27:13,752 --> 00:27:15,209
- Is that the problem?
- Yes.

539
00:27:16,072 --> 00:27:17,852
- Why?
- You can stand tall!

540
00:27:18,222 --> 00:27:19,282
What? How?

541
00:27:19,469 --> 00:27:20,651
Second thoughts?

542
00:27:21,773 --> 00:27:24,080
- Sali, this flag is the problem!
- Hey, where are you going?

543
00:27:24,081 --> 00:27:26,312
We yank it out, trample it,
and fling it to the south.

544
00:27:26,313 --> 00:27:27,466
Then we make
our way to Thomapuram.

545
00:27:27,467 --> 00:27:28,977
- That's it?
- That's it.

546
00:27:28,978 --> 00:27:30,326
- Sheesh!
- Son!

547
00:27:30,327 --> 00:27:32,142
- Son, I--
- Aashaan will sort this out now.

548
00:27:32,143 --> 00:27:34,029
Is this why you brought
us all the way here?

549
00:27:35,468 --> 00:27:36,673
So, this flag is the problem.

550
00:27:36,674 --> 00:27:39,180
He doesn't even know what's going on.
What does he think he's doing?

551
00:27:42,742 --> 00:27:44,283
- Don't pull it out...
- Oh no!

552
00:27:44,916 --> 00:27:46,456
[Stick falls to the ground]

553
00:27:50,563 --> 00:27:52,890
[Background music intensifies]

554
00:27:55,239 --> 00:27:57,613
I was going to step in.
Now, let Quintal handle this.

555
00:27:57,780 --> 00:28:01,458
How dare you try to uproot the flag
Quintal planted, you outsider mutt?

556
00:28:04,646 --> 00:28:07,320
Hey! If he wants to stay alive,
tell him to get up and run for it.

557
00:28:08,506 --> 00:28:10,477
He'll meet his end today
at the hands of Quintal.

558
00:28:10,478 --> 00:28:11,778
Aashaan!

559
00:28:12,145 --> 00:28:13,565
They're saying
you'll meet your end!

560
00:28:15,510 --> 00:28:16,623
[Bone cracks]

561
00:28:20,472 --> 00:28:23,853
That day in Thomapuram, you didn't see
Aashaan's Ravana Charitham act, right?

562
00:28:24,165 --> 00:28:25,196
No!

563
00:28:25,197 --> 00:28:26,558
Well, now you will.

564
00:28:26,559 --> 00:28:30,050
[In Kannada] Who is the ten-headed king of Lanka
who travels in the Pushpaka Vimana?

565
00:28:30,051 --> 00:28:33,208
Who is it? Who is it? Yes!
It's none other than our Ravanan!

566
00:28:33,209 --> 00:28:36,745
We invite you all to witness
the Yakshagana: The Legend of Ravana.

567
00:28:36,746 --> 00:28:40,026
[Kannada song about Ravana]

568
00:28:43,309 --> 00:28:45,615
Stone, rubble, and the bitterest wood...

569
00:28:46,723 --> 00:28:49,048
Thorn, tangled root, and the viper's hood!

570
00:28:49,049 --> 00:28:51,349
[Powerful background music]

571
00:28:54,946 --> 00:28:55,946
[Church bell]

572
00:28:58,993 --> 00:29:01,286
[Yakshagana performance sounds]

573
00:29:12,682 --> 00:29:14,235
[In Kannada] Here I come!

574
00:29:16,770 --> 00:29:18,079
Ravana, the resplendent.

575
00:29:18,302 --> 00:29:21,555
[In Kannada] Ravuther's order is to
bring him your head!

576
00:29:23,712 --> 00:29:26,462
[In Kannada] Which of my ten heads...

577
00:29:27,151 --> 00:29:29,651
does Ravuther want?

578
00:29:32,589 --> 00:29:34,395
[Powerful background music roars]

579
00:29:34,396 --> 00:29:35,415
[Shouts]

580
00:29:37,331 --> 00:29:38,578
[Boisterous laughter]

581
00:29:42,029 --> 00:29:43,029
[Hiccup]

582
00:29:46,146 --> 00:29:47,339
Hey, Church Warden!

583
00:29:48,708 --> 00:29:50,228
[Powerful background music]

584
00:29:55,077 --> 00:29:58,066
[in Kannada] You think you can
mess with me, you dog?

585
00:30:16,491 --> 00:30:17,497
[Bone cracks]

586
00:30:23,283 --> 00:30:24,742
[Thunder rumbles]

587
00:30:27,038 --> 00:30:28,285
[Boisterous laughter]

588
00:30:29,808 --> 00:30:32,560
[Powerful background music]

589
00:30:34,871 --> 00:30:35,877
Allah!

590
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:38,097
The Airborne Assault!

591
00:30:45,035 --> 00:30:46,767
[Powerful background music]

592
00:30:46,912 --> 00:30:48,579
[Shouts]

593
00:30:57,521 --> 00:30:58,800
[Roar rises]

594
00:30:59,927 --> 00:31:01,234
[Crowd cheers]

595
00:31:20,513 --> 00:31:21,519
Oh no!

596
00:31:22,983 --> 00:31:24,603
Don't you worry.

597
00:31:26,523 --> 00:31:27,530
Come on!

598
00:31:31,263 --> 00:31:32,543
[Applause]

599
00:31:50,476 --> 00:31:51,596
[Shop collapses]

600
00:31:52,239 --> 00:31:53,662
[Powerful background music rises]

601
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:09,976
One, two, three, four...

602
00:32:13,423 --> 00:32:15,052
[Boisterous laughter]

603
00:32:17,937 --> 00:32:19,804
[Music continues]

604
00:32:43,616 --> 00:32:44,623
Move!

605
00:32:45,450 --> 00:32:47,183
Oh my! Look!

606
00:32:49,536 --> 00:32:50,608
Come!

607
00:32:50,609 --> 00:32:51,889
[Shouts]

608
00:32:55,990 --> 00:32:56,990
Come!

609
00:33:09,598 --> 00:33:11,284
[Shouts]

610
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:14,380
[Fight ends]

611
00:33:14,892 --> 00:33:16,158
[Victorious shout]

612
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,098
[Crowd cheers]

613
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:31,942
Cyriac!

614
00:33:35,541 --> 00:33:37,252
Father, here's our Christopher!

615
00:33:38,351 --> 00:33:40,306
- The Christopher of our village!
- Move!

616
00:33:42,269 --> 00:33:43,689
[Powerful background music]

617
00:33:45,033 --> 00:33:46,033
Oi!

618
00:33:46,313 --> 00:33:47,484
George, my brother,

619
00:33:48,052 --> 00:33:51,012
if you try to use brute force
to plant that flag anywhere ever again...

620
00:33:51,192 --> 00:33:52,318
Don't you dare!

621
00:33:54,778 --> 00:33:57,428
- Lift him up!
- Come on! Lift him up!

622
00:33:57,622 --> 00:33:59,045
[Song begins]

623
00:34:01,988 --> 00:34:05,641
All hail Christopher of Kaaniyaar!

624
00:34:06,620 --> 00:34:10,006
All hail Christopher of Kaaniyaar!

625
00:34:11,557 --> 00:34:12,557
Put me down.

626
00:34:15,400 --> 00:34:16,407
Dear...

627
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:17,986
are you okay now?

628
00:34:18,253 --> 00:34:19,413
I'm alright.

629
00:34:37,037 --> 00:34:39,420
You are the Christopher
for whom I prayed.

630
00:34:47,983 --> 00:34:51,075
Our church isn't like
the other churches anymore.

631
00:34:51,076 --> 00:34:52,243
You know why?

632
00:34:52,779 --> 00:34:54,005
Our Christopher

633
00:34:54,366 --> 00:34:56,096
is a first-class believer.

634
00:34:56,680 --> 00:34:58,223
A pure-bred Christian!

635
00:35:03,029 --> 00:35:04,775
Now, to speak a few words,

636
00:35:04,940 --> 00:35:06,183
I invite Christopher.

637
00:35:06,488 --> 00:35:07,994
[Crowd cheering]

638
00:35:08,136 --> 00:35:09,136
Stop, stop.

639
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:13,125
Father Gregory of Thomapuram...

640
00:35:13,654 --> 00:35:15,948
spoke highly to me about
Kaaniyaar's fish curry.

641
00:35:16,118 --> 00:35:17,238
[Everyone laughs]

642
00:35:18,958 --> 00:35:20,704
The better the fish curry,

643
00:35:20,852 --> 00:35:21,859
this...

644
00:35:25,513 --> 00:35:27,053
- Pothan... Pothan!
- Yes!

645
00:35:27,433 --> 00:35:29,842
this Pothan Christopher's
blows will land harder.

646
00:35:30,125 --> 00:35:31,565
[Applause, whistles]

647
00:35:32,313 --> 00:35:35,058
A hundred times faster
than Quintal George ran,

648
00:35:35,293 --> 00:35:37,521
I'll chase the Communist goons
out of this place.

649
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:40,498
[Applause, whistles]

650
00:35:41,190 --> 00:35:44,652
From this day forth, Kaaniyaar Church's
Christopher Force stands formed.

651
00:35:44,653 --> 00:35:50,606
♪ O mighty brave one,
Battle's rising sun ♪

652
00:35:51,151 --> 00:35:56,458
♪ A burning ember...
One who is firmly enthroned.. ♪

653
00:35:56,459 --> 00:35:58,349
Hey, who the hell invited you here?

654
00:35:58,350 --> 00:36:00,396
- Joymon...
- Huh? What's wrong?

655
00:36:00,712 --> 00:36:03,452
He's not one of us.
He's one of their lot.

656
00:36:04,439 --> 00:36:05,335
Huh?

657
00:36:05,336 --> 00:36:06,976
He means...
they go to a different church.

658
00:36:07,952 --> 00:36:10,069
The church might be different.
But isn't the Lord the same?

659
00:36:10,070 --> 00:36:13,609
♪ Stream, star, and spar,
Warrior of war ♪

660
00:36:13,610 --> 00:36:16,731
♪ Eyes that fiercely glow,
Heart with fearless flow ♪

661
00:36:16,732 --> 00:36:18,594
♪ Guardian of fire and might ♪

662
00:36:18,595 --> 00:36:20,094
- What's your name, boy?
- Joy.

663
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:24,811
Boss, we're at war
with the communists, right?

664
00:36:25,232 --> 00:36:26,709
When bullets are whizzing by,

665
00:36:26,710 --> 00:36:28,914
is this the time
to argue over caste and creed?

666
00:36:30,086 --> 00:36:31,847
Come on, Joymon.
Damn right!

667
00:36:31,848 --> 00:36:33,507
[Crowd cheering]

668
00:36:36,799 --> 00:36:40,038
♪ Battles the raging tide,
Rides waves far and wide ♪

669
00:36:40,039 --> 00:36:43,172
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

670
00:36:43,173 --> 00:36:46,298
♪ Courage and might unite,
Crushing revolt in fight ♪

671
00:36:46,299 --> 00:36:49,538
♪ He leads with might,
a fearless guiding light ♪

672
00:36:49,539 --> 00:36:52,778
♪ Battles the raging tide,
Rides waves far and wide ♪

673
00:36:52,779 --> 00:36:55,912
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

674
00:36:55,913 --> 00:36:59,038
♪ Courage and might unite,
Crushing revolt in fight ♪

675
00:36:59,039 --> 00:37:02,239
♪ He leads with might,
a fearless guiding light ♪

676
00:37:02,626 --> 00:37:05,671
♪ Upon his shoulder wide,
A world of love resides ♪

677
00:37:05,672 --> 00:37:08,805
♪ Who bears this weight above?
A hero full of love ♪

678
00:37:08,806 --> 00:37:11,035
♪ Who stands guard so firm and near?
Who is the commander here? ♪

679
00:37:16,374 --> 00:37:17,937
- Chettayi?
- Hm?

680
00:37:17,938 --> 00:37:19,684
Will you teach me the airborne assault?

681
00:37:20,008 --> 00:37:21,452
- Do you want to learn it?
- Yes.

682
00:37:21,453 --> 00:37:22,506
Okay!

683
00:37:22,507 --> 00:37:24,836
♪ Who stands guard so firm and near?
Who is the commander here? ♪

684
00:37:24,837 --> 00:37:27,058
♪ He shields each life, keeps us clear,
He is the soul we revere ♪

685
00:37:27,059 --> 00:37:29,457
Even if you find yourself
face to face with a lone tusker,

686
00:37:29,458 --> 00:37:30,464
do not flinch.

687
00:37:31,086 --> 00:37:32,093
Plant your feet firmly,

688
00:37:32,687 --> 00:37:33,693
clench your fist,

689
00:37:34,006 --> 00:37:35,013
step forward.

690
00:37:35,487 --> 00:37:36,960
Strike the pressure points wisely.

691
00:37:38,813 --> 00:37:39,820
The Nape Point.

692
00:37:40,781 --> 00:37:41,787
The Temple Point.

693
00:37:43,602 --> 00:37:44,753
The Clavicle Point.

694
00:37:44,754 --> 00:37:46,452
[COMMUNIST PARTY OFFICE]

695
00:38:03,326 --> 00:38:04,838
[Bring down the Government
that goes against believers]

696
00:38:04,839 --> 00:38:06,198
[Down with Communist Rule]

697
00:38:07,176 --> 00:38:08,544
Rip that thing to shreds!

698
00:38:10,479 --> 00:38:12,705
[Tearing sound]

699
00:38:13,879 --> 00:38:15,126
[Church bell]
[Fire crackling]

700
00:38:21,820 --> 00:38:25,158
Aashaan, this is the shrine I told you
about, the one belonging to the Kurumans.

701
00:38:25,998 --> 00:38:27,340
They are well trained in combat.

702
00:38:27,820 --> 00:38:30,046
These Kurumans have mastered the art
of catching fish

703
00:38:30,047 --> 00:38:31,863
in the raging waters
of the Amaravathi River.

704
00:38:31,864 --> 00:38:33,153
It is truly a sight to behold.

705
00:38:33,526 --> 00:38:35,133
Wow, interesting.

706
00:38:36,053 --> 00:38:37,499
That's Thariyottumala Hill.

707
00:38:38,285 --> 00:38:40,251
[Background music rises]

708
00:38:41,450 --> 00:38:44,673
They're praying to keep the devils
from crossing over to this side.

709
00:38:48,686 --> 00:38:50,628
Devils, huh?

710
00:38:51,034 --> 00:38:52,034
Oh God!

711
00:38:52,891 --> 00:38:53,891
Oi!

712
00:38:55,534 --> 00:39:01,660
♪ Blossom lying on my life,
Sleeping soft, away from strife ♪

713
00:39:01,821 --> 00:39:07,747
♪ You are the warmth my thoughts pursue,
Every memory leads to you ♪

714
00:39:08,367 --> 00:39:11,566
♪ Softly, O mother's sweet child so dear ♪

715
00:39:11,567 --> 00:39:14,746
♪ Sing your lullaby for my ears to hear ♪

716
00:39:14,747 --> 00:39:17,973
♪ You are the star
in the soft silver drizzle ♪

717
00:39:17,974 --> 00:39:21,053
♪ Come down beside me,
stay just a little ♪

718
00:39:21,054 --> 00:39:24,293
♪ Rebellions swell,
the sea of fire roars and yells ♪

719
00:39:24,294 --> 00:39:27,486
♪ The sun will rise,
in iron hearts, blood burns ♪

720
00:39:27,487 --> 00:39:30,691
♪ They sow the lightning,
he halts it with his chest from striking ♪

721
00:39:30,692 --> 00:39:34,040
♪ Brave and bright,
born for the fight ♪

722
00:39:34,041 --> 00:39:37,280
♪ Battles the raging tide,
Rides waves far and wide ♪

723
00:39:37,281 --> 00:39:40,414
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

724
00:39:40,415 --> 00:39:42,157
♪ Courage and might unite ♪

725
00:39:42,158 --> 00:39:43,848
He who burned the church star today

726
00:39:43,849 --> 00:39:45,793
will not hesitate to burn men tomorrow.

727
00:39:48,361 --> 00:39:49,508
Get lost!

728
00:39:50,262 --> 00:39:53,395
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

729
00:39:53,396 --> 00:39:55,886
♪ Courage and might unite,
Crushing revolt in fight ♪

730
00:39:55,887 --> 00:39:56,893
Comrade,

731
00:39:57,139 --> 00:39:59,186
Christopher tore down our
flags at Kurishumala Hill.

732
00:39:59,423 --> 00:40:01,896
He hit me.
I can't just let this slide.

733
00:40:11,474 --> 00:40:14,713
♪ Rebellions swell,
the sea of fire roars and yells ♪

734
00:40:14,714 --> 00:40:17,864
♪ The sun will rise,
in iron hearts, blood burns ♪

735
00:40:17,865 --> 00:40:21,069
♪ They sow the lightning,
he halts it with his chest from striking ♪

736
00:40:21,070 --> 00:40:24,423
♪ Brave and bright,
born for the fight ♪

737
00:40:24,424 --> 00:40:27,663
♪ Battles the raging tide,
Rides waves far and wide ♪

738
00:40:27,664 --> 00:40:30,797
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

739
00:40:30,798 --> 00:40:33,936
♪ Courage and might unite,
Crushing revolt in fight ♪

740
00:40:33,937 --> 00:40:37,216
♪ He leads with might,
a fearless guiding light ♪

741
00:40:37,217 --> 00:40:40,441
♪ Battles the raging tide,
Rides waves far and wide ♪

742
00:40:40,442 --> 00:40:43,546
♪ Forged in strength so tight,
Charges into fight ♪

743
00:40:43,547 --> 00:40:46,769
♪ Courage and might unite,
Crushing revolt in fight ♪

744
00:40:46,770 --> 00:40:49,970
♪ He leads with might,
a fearless guiding light ♪

745
00:40:51,423 --> 00:40:53,042
Hey, guy with the moustache, smile!

746
00:40:53,043 --> 00:40:54,473
You just stick to taking pictures.

747
00:40:54,700 --> 00:40:56,220
[Girls laughing]

748
00:40:56,221 --> 00:40:58,149
Don't laugh too much.
He's my friend!

749
00:40:58,510 --> 00:41:00,550
All of you, smile!

750
00:41:01,452 --> 00:41:02,739
[Camera shutter clicks]

751
00:41:02,740 --> 00:41:04,732
[Song ends]

752
00:41:06,009 --> 00:41:07,095
[Bicycle chain rattles]

753
00:41:07,724 --> 00:41:11,369
An emergency meeting of the Home Department
was held in the Chief Minister's chamber.

754
00:41:12,233 --> 00:41:15,800
The Liberation Struggle against the
Communist government is intensifying.

755
00:41:16,736 --> 00:41:19,180
To confront the struggle
and Christopher Force,

756
00:41:19,181 --> 00:41:21,745
a decision has been taken
to appoint Special Officers

757
00:41:22,171 --> 00:41:25,068
in zones prone to conflict.

758
00:41:26,343 --> 00:41:27,994
But sir, how do you know all this?

759
00:41:28,546 --> 00:41:32,393
While your police and government
sit there reading classified documents,

760
00:41:32,676 --> 00:41:34,448
I hear it right here.

761
00:41:35,187 --> 00:41:37,231
That's Eapen Daniel for you!

762
00:41:37,232 --> 00:41:38,348
[Typewriter clacking]

763
00:41:38,481 --> 00:41:40,408
I might be under suspension now

764
00:41:40,731 --> 00:41:43,032
but I have walked the
halls of that South Block

765
00:41:43,033 --> 00:41:45,481
many a time as the
Additional Home Secretary, haven't I?

766
00:41:50,365 --> 00:41:53,444
This decision to appoint
Special Officers is all well and good.

767
00:41:54,068 --> 00:41:55,131
It's a good move.

768
00:41:55,132 --> 00:41:56,771
[Typewriter clacking]
But...

769
00:41:57,177 --> 00:41:58,572
your list!

770
00:41:58,661 --> 00:41:59,836
[Radio tuning static]

771
00:41:59,837 --> 00:42:01,218
I cannot accept it.

772
00:42:05,166 --> 00:42:09,285
For the Kaaniyaar Division,
as Special Officer, I want this man.

773
00:42:09,394 --> 00:42:10,741
[Ominous music]

774
00:42:13,213 --> 00:42:14,908
- Sir, him?
- Yes.

775
00:42:15,391 --> 00:42:18,508
The mastermind of the great
rebellion during the partition.

776
00:42:19,302 --> 00:42:23,008
The architect of the Rawalpet massacre
where seven thousand people fell dead.

777
00:42:23,442 --> 00:42:25,426
In 1946,

778
00:42:25,989 --> 00:42:27,613
when Ginna called for direct action

779
00:42:27,614 --> 00:42:31,248
against Indian civilians
in a secret meeting,

780
00:42:31,572 --> 00:42:33,099
he was the only non-politican present.

781
00:42:33,614 --> 00:42:34,853
Rairu Ramanna!

782
00:42:34,854 --> 00:42:36,054
[Ominous music]

783
00:42:37,880 --> 00:42:39,719
The next I heard of him

784
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:42,043
was after last year's
[Telephone rings]

785
00:42:42,044 --> 00:42:44,045
Rajanathapuram riots in Tamil Nadu...

786
00:42:44,279 --> 00:42:46,468
[Telephone rings]
Sir... Sir, but?

787
00:42:46,582 --> 00:42:47,770
It's decided!

788
00:42:47,771 --> 00:42:48,771
[Telephone receiver lifted]

789
00:42:50,402 --> 00:42:51,409
Hello.

790
00:42:51,949 --> 00:42:53,288
Hello, Eapen Sir.

791
00:42:54,048 --> 00:42:57,356
The five title deeds you asked about...
the agreements have been completed.

792
00:42:57,357 --> 00:42:58,385
And the sixth one?

793
00:42:58,529 --> 00:42:59,875
There's a small complication...

794
00:42:59,876 --> 00:43:01,608
- Oh!
- Nothing serious, Sir.

795
00:43:01,732 --> 00:43:03,835
The woman who owns the
five acres by the river...

796
00:43:03,836 --> 00:43:05,223
She's a bit of a headache.

797
00:43:05,750 --> 00:43:07,529
We must speak to her
and convince her.

798
00:43:08,524 --> 00:43:09,537
I'll handle that, Sir.

799
00:43:09,932 --> 00:43:12,031
- Yeah.
- And, sir...

800
00:43:12,336 --> 00:43:14,235
About that part payment...

801
00:43:14,584 --> 00:43:17,421
When I tell you to arrange six title deeds,
I mean six.

802
00:43:17,422 --> 00:43:18,510
Five is not enough.

803
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:21,056
- How many families live in Kunnumpuram?
- Move aside. Go!

804
00:43:21,057 --> 00:43:22,801
110 in total.

805
00:43:22,802 --> 00:43:24,267
Ah, 110.

806
00:43:24,366 --> 00:43:25,799
They're all settlers.

807
00:43:26,107 --> 00:43:28,433
Just six of them have title deeds.

808
00:43:28,573 --> 00:43:29,631
Right?

809
00:43:29,632 --> 00:43:31,126
You have secured five already.

810
00:43:31,127 --> 00:43:34,907
And you expect Eapen's game to work
only if I pay for the sixth?

811
00:43:35,096 --> 00:43:36,102
Oh no...

812
00:43:36,605 --> 00:43:38,055
- No, Sir, that's not it...
- Idiot!

813
00:43:38,226 --> 00:43:39,346
[Telephone receiver placed down]

814
00:43:41,347 --> 00:43:43,280
Announcement]
Come, witness and be enthralled!

815
00:43:44,018 --> 00:43:48,155
The revolutionary social
drama you awaited.

816
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:51,489
K.P.A.C.'s
'You Made Me a Communist.'

817
00:43:51,899 --> 00:43:55,002
An epic saga of the peasant uprising...
against the tyranny of feudalism.

818
00:43:55,676 --> 00:43:57,088
'You Made Me a Communist.'

819
00:43:57,514 --> 00:43:59,094
Come, witness...

820
00:43:59,779 --> 00:44:03,934
This single play provided fertile soil
for the Communist Party to grow in Kerala.

821
00:44:03,935 --> 00:44:05,840
That play is like a narcotic, isn't it?

822
00:44:06,081 --> 00:44:07,398
Everyone who sees it

823
00:44:07,399 --> 00:44:09,758
forgets the Lord Almighty
and chants "Inquilab".

824
00:44:10,500 --> 00:44:12,419
Two, even three shows a day!

825
00:44:12,533 --> 00:44:14,986
Isn't K.P.A.C spewing
venom across the land?

826
00:44:15,445 --> 00:44:17,726
Their first play is happening in
the Ayyathankovil region.

827
00:44:17,853 --> 00:44:20,240
The second is at the foothills
of our Kurishumala.

828
00:44:20,571 --> 00:44:22,762
That girl from Kunnumpuram,
is their lead actress.

829
00:44:22,763 --> 00:44:23,982
Huh? Which girl?

830
00:44:24,386 --> 00:44:26,718
Elsy's elder sister was married
off to someone in Kannur, right?

831
00:44:26,719 --> 00:44:28,325
- Yes.
- Her daughter, Rebecca.

832
00:44:28,326 --> 00:44:30,239
Hmph!
She did all her studying here, didn't she?

833
00:44:31,139 --> 00:44:33,453
A hundred others will gather
just to get a glimpse of her.

834
00:44:34,846 --> 00:44:37,933
As it is, the lads walk about with
that red book clutched in their hands.

835
00:44:38,080 --> 00:44:40,200
Now with this on top of it all,
that's just perfect.

836
00:44:41,159 --> 00:44:44,065
After hearing all this, why are you just
standing there silently, Pothan?

837
00:44:44,066 --> 00:44:46,699
Now they're going to perform
a play under our very noses.

838
00:44:46,818 --> 00:44:47,952
We cannot let this slide.

839
00:44:48,728 --> 00:44:50,404
You must thrash them
and drive them out!

840
00:44:52,353 --> 00:44:53,360
For what?

841
00:44:55,352 --> 00:44:56,358
Father,

842
00:44:56,510 --> 00:44:58,753
whoever stands against the Church,
no matter who he is,

843
00:44:58,754 --> 00:45:00,812
I will smash his kneecaps
and bring him down.

844
00:45:00,813 --> 00:45:01,820
That is my job.

845
00:45:02,706 --> 00:45:04,722
I am the Christopher
of the Kunnumpuram Church.

846
00:45:04,723 --> 00:45:06,210
Not some thug-for-hire!

847
00:45:07,792 --> 00:45:10,250
Moreover, is a play really
a worthy opponent for us, Father?

848
00:45:10,794 --> 00:45:12,237
After all, isn't it a form of art?

849
00:45:12,238 --> 00:45:14,371
You don't know it!
It is the deadliest of poisons, I tell you!

850
00:45:14,372 --> 00:45:15,652
Hey, Kuncheriya!

851
00:45:16,119 --> 00:45:17,210
My child,

852
00:45:17,211 --> 00:45:19,083
to say 'You Made Me a Communist',

853
00:45:19,333 --> 00:45:21,462
is to say; you have made
me an enemy of God.

854
00:45:21,463 --> 00:45:23,359
Made me a non-believer,
that is its meaning.

855
00:45:23,360 --> 00:45:25,631
Do you know why they've staged
this drama at Kurishumala?

856
00:45:25,632 --> 00:45:29,081
It is to take revenge for tearing down
the flag they hoisted there.

857
00:45:29,082 --> 00:45:30,082
Understood?

858
00:45:32,272 --> 00:45:34,618
No matter what, their play
will not happen at Kurishumala.

859
00:45:35,713 --> 00:45:37,926
You have the word of
Kunnumpuram Church's Christopher.

860
00:45:38,168 --> 00:45:39,568
[Hopeful background music begins]

861
00:45:41,120 --> 00:45:42,319
Any doubts?

862
00:45:42,791 --> 00:45:44,312
- Eh?
- Do you?

863
00:45:45,396 --> 00:45:46,433
No.

864
00:45:46,434 --> 00:45:47,793
So then, Kurishumala can wait.

865
00:45:48,366 --> 00:45:49,659
The first play...

866
00:45:50,738 --> 00:45:52,094
at Ayyathankovil.

867
00:45:54,281 --> 00:45:56,179
The performance you have
all been anxiously awaiting,

868
00:45:56,180 --> 00:45:57,685
K.P.A.C.'s revolutionary drama,

869
00:45:57,686 --> 00:45:59,735
will commence at ten o'clock sharp.

870
00:45:59,867 --> 00:46:02,280
This play is brought to you
with the patronage of

871
00:46:02,620 --> 00:46:05,813
the honourable Lord Anandan
of Poovathin Maalika.

872
00:46:06,501 --> 00:46:08,714
Master, I saw the actress!

873
00:46:09,020 --> 00:46:10,790
I saw our Rebecca!

874
00:46:10,791 --> 00:46:12,000
[Playful background music begins]

875
00:46:12,001 --> 00:46:14,785
- Ah, what is it, Rajappan?
- I saw her, Master, I saw her.

876
00:46:14,786 --> 00:46:16,687
- And?
- Oh, she is a divine maiden!

877
00:46:18,122 --> 00:46:20,081
Like a rich, red slab of halwa.

878
00:46:21,225 --> 00:46:23,297
- But your intentions won't succeed.
- Eh?

879
00:46:23,869 --> 00:46:26,102
If that's the case, why did
I spend the money? Tell me!

880
00:46:26,103 --> 00:46:28,893
That's not it, Master. She says
she needs neither food nor rest.

881
00:46:28,894 --> 00:46:30,260
She's already begun her make-up.

882
00:46:32,672 --> 00:46:34,594
- Aashaan, shall I get the country bomb?
- No.

883
00:46:34,595 --> 00:46:36,145
- Not now.
- How about some peanuts then?

884
00:46:36,382 --> 00:46:37,723
- Nah.
- Don't want any?

885
00:46:39,704 --> 00:46:41,567
Hello checking, hello checking...

886
00:46:41,952 --> 00:46:42,992
Huh! Rebecca!

887
00:46:43,682 --> 00:46:47,942
Master, she's gone into the toilet.

888
00:46:49,064 --> 00:46:50,719
[Lustful music rises]

889
00:46:54,311 --> 00:46:55,447
[Power goes out]

890
00:46:55,448 --> 00:46:56,909
The lights have gone out!

891
00:46:56,910 --> 00:46:58,213
How about throwing the bomb now?

892
00:46:58,214 --> 00:46:59,908
It will come back now.
Let the play begin.

893
00:46:59,909 --> 00:47:01,158
Let's throw it then.

894
00:47:01,159 --> 00:47:02,679
[Power returns]

895
00:47:03,273 --> 00:47:04,273
Ah! Look!

896
00:47:05,775 --> 00:47:06,812
[Woman] Oh my God!

897
00:47:06,813 --> 00:47:07,813
Oh no!

898
00:47:08,279 --> 00:47:11,645
Somebody, come quickly!
Oh, no... Rebecca! Oh, no!

899
00:47:11,646 --> 00:47:12,988
Hey low-lives!

900
00:47:12,989 --> 00:47:15,602
If the Master says he'll take
the actress, he will take her!

901
00:47:15,695 --> 00:47:16,852
They've taken the actress!

902
00:47:17,105 --> 00:47:19,325
- Hey, don't embarrass me!
- She doesn't know us well enough!

903
00:47:19,795 --> 00:47:21,420
Aashaan! What about the bomb?

904
00:47:23,401 --> 00:47:25,562
[Exciting background music begins]

905
00:47:26,220 --> 00:47:27,368
[Master Anandan's property]

906
00:47:30,013 --> 00:47:31,013
Rebecca!

907
00:47:36,887 --> 00:47:37,941
Oi!

908
00:47:37,942 --> 00:47:40,113
Master, some scoundrel is following us.

909
00:47:40,114 --> 00:47:41,448
- Step on it!
- Stop the car!

910
00:47:42,353 --> 00:47:43,519
What the hell are you doing?

911
00:47:44,353 --> 00:47:45,559
He must be here for the show!

912
00:47:45,560 --> 00:47:47,410
- Cover me, Thankappan!
- Stop the car!

913
00:47:47,411 --> 00:47:48,846
Get it over with, Master!

914
00:47:49,789 --> 00:47:51,113
Don't fall into gutters!

915
00:47:52,283 --> 00:47:54,136
[Remix of a vintage rhythmic song]

916
00:47:54,476 --> 00:47:56,335
Don't get your claws out, pussycat!

917
00:47:59,274 --> 00:48:00,684
Get lost!

918
00:48:02,587 --> 00:48:05,748
I've been following you around
carrying this bundle!

919
00:48:05,749 --> 00:48:08,226
Did I ask you to
follow me, you dog?

920
00:48:08,227 --> 00:48:10,914
After shaking your backside
and winking all over town,

921
00:48:10,915 --> 00:48:13,680
now you're playing the saint,
you bloody...!!!

922
00:48:15,066 --> 00:48:17,555
- Don't waste time, Master!
- Oh no!

923
00:48:18,235 --> 00:48:19,371
What is it?

924
00:48:19,372 --> 00:48:20,858
Did a civet just land on top?

925
00:48:21,387 --> 00:48:22,591
Thankappan!

926
00:48:22,592 --> 00:48:23,716
Oh no!

927
00:48:24,394 --> 00:48:27,238
- Master!
- Yes, I am the Master!

928
00:48:27,815 --> 00:48:28,859
Salutations!

929
00:48:30,555 --> 00:48:31,588
Oh my!

930
00:48:32,273 --> 00:48:34,125
- Slowly! Slowly!
- Get out, you bloody Master!

931
00:48:34,126 --> 00:48:35,126
Oh no!

932
00:48:36,128 --> 00:48:37,128
[Slap]

933
00:48:37,793 --> 00:48:38,813
[Slap]

934
00:48:39,762 --> 00:48:42,115
[Romantic background music begins]

935
00:48:47,578 --> 00:48:48,578
Don't cry.

936
00:48:49,039 --> 00:48:51,088
Nothing happened to you.
Don't be afraid.

937
00:48:56,376 --> 00:48:58,872
Christopher, if you are to throw a bomb,
then throw it.

938
00:48:58,873 --> 00:49:00,259
Do not make fools of people.

939
00:49:00,260 --> 00:49:02,820
You ought to have thought
her abduction worked in our favour, no?

940
00:49:02,821 --> 00:49:04,685
The play would have come
to a halt right then and there!

941
00:49:04,818 --> 00:49:06,352
You ruined a perfectly
good chance, Christopher!

942
00:49:06,353 --> 00:49:08,375
Father, in the very shadow
of the Church,

943
00:49:08,687 --> 00:49:10,249
with hundreds watching,

944
00:49:10,574 --> 00:49:13,861
a scoundrel abducts a girl
and attempts to violate her.

945
00:49:14,134 --> 00:49:16,466
If a man sees that and does
nothing, is he a Christian, Father?

946
00:49:16,467 --> 00:49:17,521
You tell me!

947
00:49:17,522 --> 00:49:19,633
When we die and go before the Lord,
won't He ask us?

948
00:49:19,634 --> 00:49:20,641
Won't He? Tell me!

949
00:49:20,854 --> 00:49:23,365
- Ah. That's true.
- Ah!

950
00:49:23,366 --> 00:49:24,615
That's all well and good.

951
00:49:24,616 --> 00:49:26,000
But they're already at Kurishumala,

952
00:49:26,001 --> 00:49:28,887
- building the stage for tomorrow's play.
- Ah! That's right.

953
00:49:28,994 --> 00:49:30,637
Let them build it, Kuncheria.

954
00:49:31,115 --> 00:49:32,122
Christopher?

955
00:49:37,402 --> 00:49:39,863
Tonight is the last night for KPAC,

956
00:49:40,154 --> 00:49:41,160
on our soil.

957
00:49:41,407 --> 00:49:42,624
You can be sure of that!

958
00:49:42,625 --> 00:49:44,252
[Exciting background music]

959
00:49:44,830 --> 00:49:46,018
[Crowd cheering]

960
00:49:46,019 --> 00:49:47,025
[Loud horn blares]

961
00:49:52,478 --> 00:49:53,651
[Cheers grow louder]

962
00:50:00,872 --> 00:50:02,522
Hey, Aashaan!

963
00:50:02,752 --> 00:50:04,034
- Hmm?
- Who's that?

964
00:50:04,255 --> 00:50:05,286
- I don't know.
- Eh?

965
00:50:05,287 --> 00:50:06,926
- Focus on what you came for.
- Ah.

966
00:50:09,597 --> 00:50:11,423
[Soft background music begins]

967
00:50:13,955 --> 00:50:15,165
Listen, Rebecca...

968
00:50:15,483 --> 00:50:17,910
That guy who rescued
you last night is out there.

969
00:50:18,570 --> 00:50:21,207
[Romantic background music
slowly swells]

970
00:50:24,444 --> 00:50:25,450
Hey?

971
00:50:26,270 --> 00:50:27,270
Rebecca?

972
00:50:33,207 --> 00:50:34,909
Rebecca!

973
00:50:41,326 --> 00:50:43,305
[Romantic background music rises]

974
00:51:12,728 --> 00:51:14,039
[Romantic background music fades]

975
00:51:18,100 --> 00:51:21,047
Yesterday, it was this man...
who saved my life.

976
00:51:21,553 --> 00:51:23,717
Just as I was lamenting
that I never learnt

977
00:51:23,718 --> 00:51:26,392
the name of the man who
disappeared in a flash,

978
00:51:26,393 --> 00:51:28,423
I came to know that you
were standing right here.

979
00:51:28,556 --> 00:51:31,615
So I had to come over
and thank you, right?

980
00:51:33,225 --> 00:51:35,337
Comrade, could you please
come up to the stage?

981
00:51:35,338 --> 00:51:36,471
Or it'll be a real hassle!

982
00:51:36,472 --> 00:51:38,202
Chetta, will you please
come to the stage?

983
00:51:38,203 --> 00:51:39,209
Let's talk over there.

984
00:51:39,971 --> 00:51:42,438
Aashaan, get on to the stage quickly,
or our backs will break.

985
00:51:44,623 --> 00:51:45,626
Rebecca!

986
00:51:46,003 --> 00:51:49,534
Give me a kiss, darling!

987
00:51:50,353 --> 00:51:52,318
[Bone cracks]
How dare you!

988
00:51:54,310 --> 00:51:55,334
Scoundrel!

989
00:51:55,335 --> 00:51:56,822
[Romantic background music swells]

990
00:51:59,048 --> 00:52:00,205
All of you, move aside!

991
00:52:02,229 --> 00:52:03,664
Saali, give me a hand!

992
00:52:03,842 --> 00:52:05,222
Move.

993
00:52:10,681 --> 00:52:11,688
Move!

994
00:52:15,415 --> 00:52:16,421
I said, stand aside!

995
00:52:20,168 --> 00:52:21,575
Move! All of you, stand aside.

996
00:52:43,487 --> 00:52:45,787
[Romantic background music fades]

997
00:52:45,981 --> 00:52:47,923
So he saved you again, huh?

998
00:52:48,770 --> 00:52:50,910
- He's quite impressive!
- Shut up!

999
00:52:52,163 --> 00:52:53,833
Have these people gone mad?

1000
00:52:53,834 --> 00:52:55,346
Have they never
seen actors before?

1001
00:52:55,347 --> 00:52:56,353
Morons!

1002
00:53:00,961 --> 00:53:02,481
"Harahara Reddy Bailaattam"

1003
00:53:02,908 --> 00:53:05,003
Have you heard of it?

1004
00:53:05,189 --> 00:53:06,195
Huh?

1005
00:53:06,708 --> 00:53:07,808
Huh?

1006
00:53:08,728 --> 00:53:09,875
How would you have heard?

1007
00:53:10,770 --> 00:53:12,295
It is a Yakshagana Theatre Troupe.

1008
00:53:12,762 --> 00:53:13,954
"Ravana Charitham,"

1009
00:53:13,955 --> 00:53:16,901
has been staged over 500 times
in Malabar and Karnataka.

1010
00:53:17,022 --> 00:53:18,201
- How many?
- 500.

1011
00:53:18,202 --> 00:53:19,208
Ah, 500!

1012
00:53:19,881 --> 00:53:20,888
Who plays Ravana?

1013
00:53:21,382 --> 00:53:22,655
- Who?
- Who?

1014
00:53:23,280 --> 00:53:24,365
I do!

1015
00:53:26,341 --> 00:53:28,447
And not a single person
has come after me!

1016
00:53:28,988 --> 00:53:30,887
If someone comes,
I will smash his kneecaps.

1017
00:53:30,888 --> 00:53:32,262
- They know that!
- It is time.

1018
00:53:32,263 --> 00:53:33,861
- Any doubt?
- Then make the call.

1019
00:53:33,862 --> 00:53:35,621
Rebecca, isn't your makeup done?

1020
00:53:35,622 --> 00:53:38,120
Oh, I'm ready.
I just need to change out of this costume.

1021
00:53:38,121 --> 00:53:39,281
Then go and get changed.

1022
00:53:39,604 --> 00:53:41,686
Move those chairs.
Let us begin.

1023
00:53:41,687 --> 00:53:44,580
- What about him?
- It's okay. Just tell him.

1024
00:53:44,581 --> 00:53:47,100
Art-lovers, at precisely
10 o'clock,

1025
00:53:47,101 --> 00:53:50,460
the play, 'You Made Me a Communist',
presented by K. P.A.C.,

1026
00:53:50,461 --> 00:53:51,908
will commence on this stage.

1027
00:53:54,613 --> 00:53:56,394
"Ravana Charitham"...
I've seen it.

1028
00:53:57,048 --> 00:53:58,396
Huh? When?

1029
00:53:59,808 --> 00:54:01,343
A while ago.

1030
00:54:01,499 --> 00:54:02,674
And where was that?

1031
00:54:02,888 --> 00:54:03,928
- Bantadukka.
- Huh?

1032
00:54:04,607 --> 00:54:07,233
Keramane Shivarama Hegde,
in the role of Ravana.

1033
00:54:07,322 --> 00:54:08,653
There is that one line in it…

1034
00:54:08,852 --> 00:54:11,027
[In Kannada] I am Ravana! Of the battlefield

1035
00:54:11,028 --> 00:54:13,465
- The valiant, the fierce, the invincible!
- The valiant, the fierce, the invincible!

1036
00:54:13,466 --> 00:54:14,466
Oh dear...

1037
00:54:17,814 --> 00:54:19,721
[Soft background music rises]

1038
00:54:24,675 --> 00:54:25,682
I...

1039
00:54:28,302 --> 00:54:30,836
Hey, leaving already,
valiant, fierce, invincible one?

1040
00:54:31,385 --> 00:54:33,623
[Romantic background music swells]

1041
00:54:39,182 --> 00:54:41,082
[Romantic background music fades]

1042
00:54:41,222 --> 00:54:42,561
Aashaan, where have you been?

1043
00:54:42,562 --> 00:54:43,666
You've been gone for a while!

1044
00:54:43,667 --> 00:54:46,088
Any longer, and I'd have
thrown that country bomb myself.

1045
00:54:46,089 --> 00:54:47,095
Hey!

1046
00:54:47,342 --> 00:54:48,348
Hmm?

1047
00:54:50,601 --> 00:54:52,254
[Playful background music rises]

1048
00:54:52,415 --> 00:54:53,547
- Come...
- Eh?

1049
00:54:54,041 --> 00:54:55,280
Come? Where to?

1050
00:54:55,715 --> 00:54:56,722
Get over here!

1051
00:54:57,054 --> 00:54:59,327
[Audience applauds]

1052
00:55:03,855 --> 00:55:08,559
♪ O girl, who casts your eyes
upon the golden sickle of a moon ♪

1053
00:55:08,560 --> 00:55:13,200
♪ O girl, who stands somber
in the flowery shade of that tree ♪

1054
00:55:16,712 --> 00:55:19,322
You said we'd throw it in a deserted spot,
but this place is crawling with people.

1055
00:55:21,104 --> 00:55:22,111
Come on.

1056
00:55:23,461 --> 00:55:27,292
Hey, you must come over to my house
at the fall of dusk.

1057
00:55:27,449 --> 00:55:28,461
- For what?
- Ha!

1058
00:55:28,462 --> 00:55:31,577
Tell your old man that you're
coming to fetch water for me.

1059
00:55:31,729 --> 00:55:34,292
Since I love you,
caste differences don't matter.

1060
00:55:34,293 --> 00:55:36,093
Move aside, Lord!

1061
00:55:37,561 --> 00:55:39,917
I'm a servant, not a slave!

1062
00:55:40,401 --> 00:55:42,687
[Stage music intensifies]

1063
00:55:50,474 --> 00:55:52,608
[Crying on stage]

1064
00:55:54,267 --> 00:55:56,390
Maala, are you crying?

1065
00:55:58,390 --> 00:55:59,418
- Here...
- Ah.

1066
00:56:01,604 --> 00:56:03,327
Why are you crying, Maala?

1067
00:56:07,382 --> 00:56:08,443
I won't cry anymore.

1068
00:56:08,710 --> 00:56:10,410
[Emotional background music begins]

1069
00:56:13,522 --> 00:56:14,862
[Stifled sob]

1070
00:56:15,804 --> 00:56:17,394
Are you crying, Seethamma?

1071
00:56:28,589 --> 00:56:31,029
No, little one.
I won't cry anymore.

1072
00:56:33,782 --> 00:56:35,535
Seethamma, where is Mother?

1073
00:56:35,809 --> 00:56:36,809
Maala...

1074
00:56:38,064 --> 00:56:40,055
Don't you know
how your mother died?

1075
00:56:45,308 --> 00:56:46,308
[Thunder crashes on stage]

1076
00:56:48,477 --> 00:56:50,449
Yes. I saw it happen.

1077
00:56:53,567 --> 00:56:55,546
[Ominous background music rises]

1078
00:57:03,939 --> 00:57:08,167
I saw that lord beating
my mother to death.

1079
00:57:08,409 --> 00:57:10,182
[Emotional background music swells]

1080
00:57:10,565 --> 00:57:13,327
I saw that lord beating my mother
and her people to death!

1081
00:57:14,466 --> 00:57:15,466
Move aside!

1082
00:57:15,597 --> 00:57:16,677
Mother!

1083
00:57:17,245 --> 00:57:18,252
Mother?

1084
00:57:20,189 --> 00:57:21,189
Move aside!

1085
00:57:23,375 --> 00:57:24,609
No... Father!

1086
00:57:25,621 --> 00:57:27,447
Release my father!

1087
00:57:27,662 --> 00:57:28,788
[Screams]

1088
00:57:29,427 --> 00:57:30,966
Son!

1089
00:57:34,701 --> 00:57:36,067
[Screams]

1090
00:57:37,079 --> 00:57:39,926
My child, this is the life we lead.

1091
00:57:41,627 --> 00:57:43,872
If we stand firm on our own soil,

1092
00:57:43,995 --> 00:57:46,041
- the lords will slaughter us!
- Oh gods,

1093
00:57:46,232 --> 00:57:48,316
Are you not seeing this?

1094
00:57:49,097 --> 00:57:50,501
My child!

1095
00:57:50,502 --> 00:57:52,022
Mother Kaali!

1096
00:57:52,023 --> 00:57:54,097
[Intensely emotional
background music rises]

1097
00:57:54,698 --> 00:57:57,430
Pillai! Pillai!

1098
00:57:58,051 --> 00:57:59,824
You must be there, Pillai!

1099
00:57:59,825 --> 00:58:03,111
You must guard the forest and its folk!

1100
00:58:06,224 --> 00:58:08,347
Kelu Pappa!

1101
00:58:09,877 --> 00:58:11,624
I want to lift this

1102
00:58:11,777 --> 00:58:13,150
and hold it high!

1103
00:58:14,835 --> 00:58:17,132
- Long live the revolution!
- Long live the revolution!

1104
00:58:17,133 --> 00:58:18,561
Long live the revolution!

1105
00:58:18,731 --> 00:58:31,034
Long live the revolution!

1106
00:58:31,035 --> 00:58:33,044
[Intensely emotional
background music fades]

1107
00:58:34,464 --> 00:58:37,208
I was adamant that I'll go home
only after seeing you, Chechi.

1108
00:58:37,411 --> 00:58:40,024
- Otherwise mom wouldn't--
- Are you happy now?

1109
00:58:40,444 --> 00:58:41,444
Yes.

1110
00:58:42,296 --> 00:58:44,660
Auntie, you may leave now.

1111
00:58:44,858 --> 00:58:46,291
Don't let the church folk see you.

1112
00:58:46,484 --> 00:58:48,085
You go ahead, I'll follow.

1113
00:58:48,645 --> 00:58:50,680
- Hey, be careful on your way!
- Okay, sister.

1114
00:58:51,032 --> 00:58:52,412
- Come back soon.
- Yes.

1115
00:58:53,973 --> 00:58:56,289
[Gentle background music]

1116
00:58:58,230 --> 00:58:59,237
Did you enjoy the play?

1117
00:59:03,667 --> 00:59:05,307
[Bus engine starts]

1118
00:59:06,532 --> 00:59:07,539
Comrade?

1119
00:59:09,131 --> 00:59:10,382
The bus is leaving.

1120
00:59:10,537 --> 00:59:12,797
You go ahead.
I'm going to my aunt's place.

1121
00:59:13,043 --> 00:59:15,036
Take care.
See you tomorrow at Alappuzha!

1122
00:59:15,283 --> 00:59:16,290
Yeah.

1123
00:59:19,090 --> 00:59:20,859
Your name is Krishna Pillai, right?

1124
00:59:22,406 --> 00:59:24,110
Aashaan, don't be scared.

1125
00:59:24,943 --> 00:59:25,943
Run!

1126
00:59:26,092 --> 00:59:27,532
[Rapid footsteps]

1127
00:59:30,301 --> 00:59:32,635
[Oars slicing through water]

1128
00:59:35,919 --> 00:59:38,925
I'm aware of
Christopher Krishna Pillai's story.

1129
00:59:40,390 --> 00:59:42,410
Our party is present all over Kerala.

1130
00:59:44,059 --> 00:59:45,066
Don't worry,

1131
00:59:45,278 --> 00:59:46,644
I won't tell anyone.

1132
00:59:47,686 --> 00:59:51,665
Communism isn't about excluding
those with ideological differences,

1133
00:59:51,666 --> 00:59:53,257
but embracing them.

1134
00:59:53,352 --> 00:59:55,132
[Hopeful background music]

1135
01:00:04,435 --> 01:00:05,895
What are you thinking?

1136
01:00:09,011 --> 01:00:10,104
[Rain pours with thunder]

1137
01:00:10,592 --> 01:00:11,673
[Police Station, Thomapuram]

1138
01:00:11,674 --> 01:00:14,674
[In broken Malayalam] Just speaking ill
about noblemen isn't enough...

1139
01:00:14,996 --> 01:00:16,205
There should be an eyewitness.

1140
01:00:17,375 --> 01:00:18,642
Eye witness.

1141
01:00:18,643 --> 01:00:19,889
[Ominous music]

1142
01:00:21,049 --> 01:00:22,208
Did you see it?

1143
01:00:23,295 --> 01:00:24,302
No.

1144
01:00:25,135 --> 01:00:26,142
Did you see it?

1145
01:00:27,377 --> 01:00:28,390
Did you?

1146
01:00:29,349 --> 01:00:30,909
[Cruel laughter]

1147
01:00:32,047 --> 01:00:33,074
Bloody dogs!

1148
01:00:35,188 --> 01:00:36,195
I saw it.

1149
01:00:36,792 --> 01:00:38,597
[Ominous music swells]

1150
01:00:39,085 --> 01:00:40,379
Seethamma?

1151
01:00:47,384 --> 01:00:50,285
I saw the Lord beating my
mother and her people to death.

1152
01:00:51,997 --> 01:00:53,595
You slave dogs!

1153
01:00:55,799 --> 01:01:00,744
Has your blood grown so insolent that
you dare trespass upon Pattelar's land?

1154
01:01:01,359 --> 01:01:02,359
This...

1155
01:01:02,631 --> 01:01:04,591
This is the land we sowed,
watered, and harvested!

1156
01:01:04,751 --> 01:01:06,765
- What?
- Why, Sir?

1157
01:01:08,538 --> 01:01:10,389
Why has it been divided
with boundaries drawn?

1158
01:01:10,390 --> 01:01:12,009
Shut your mouth, you outcaste!

1159
01:01:12,876 --> 01:01:13,883
Mother!

1160
01:01:14,108 --> 01:01:15,775
What gives you the nerve
to speak back,

1161
01:01:15,776 --> 01:01:17,217
you filthy slave!

1162
01:01:17,676 --> 01:01:19,542
[Mournful background music rises]

1163
01:01:22,254 --> 01:01:23,260
You saw it?

1164
01:01:32,851 --> 01:01:33,858
Did you see it?

1165
01:01:34,344 --> 01:01:35,350
I saw it.

1166
01:01:38,190 --> 01:01:39,621
Seethamma!

1167
01:01:41,650 --> 01:01:42,669
[Shouts]

1168
01:01:48,885 --> 01:01:50,972
You dare trespass
into Pattelar Saab's land

1169
01:01:51,639 --> 01:01:53,346
and spew such nonsense?

1170
01:01:53,749 --> 01:01:54,769
[Spits in contempt]

1171
01:01:55,481 --> 01:01:57,258
And you dare lie to the police?

1172
01:02:00,711 --> 01:02:02,211
Bloody scum!

1173
01:02:03,205 --> 01:02:04,931
[Mournful background music rises]

1174
01:02:09,020 --> 01:02:10,106
Seethamma?

1175
01:02:10,492 --> 01:02:11,598
Seethamma?

1176
01:02:12,264 --> 01:02:13,864
[Rain pours with thunder]

1177
01:02:25,925 --> 01:02:26,932
Sir!

1178
01:02:27,267 --> 01:02:29,022
The girl isn't breathing, Sir!

1179
01:02:30,060 --> 01:02:31,074
My child!

1180
01:02:31,181 --> 01:02:33,314
[Mournful background music rises

1181
01:02:34,432 --> 01:02:35,865
O my Lord!

1182
01:02:37,126 --> 01:02:38,937
Seetha, my dear!

1183
01:02:38,938 --> 01:02:39,938
My child!

1184
01:02:50,018 --> 01:02:51,049
Hey!

1185
01:02:51,050 --> 01:02:52,423
[Mournful background music fades]

1186
01:02:53,351 --> 01:02:54,358
Hey!

1187
01:02:54,926 --> 01:02:56,011
Is the wedding over?

1188
01:02:56,012 --> 01:02:57,274
The wedding is tomorrow!

1189
01:02:57,680 --> 01:02:59,220
Today's the ritual at the temple.

1190
01:02:59,466 --> 01:03:00,735
Will you come, Christopher?

1191
01:03:00,736 --> 01:03:01,858
Of course I'll be there!

1192
01:03:01,859 --> 01:03:03,246
Alright, see you there then.

1193
01:03:04,601 --> 01:03:06,221
[Tender background music]

1194
01:03:09,700 --> 01:03:11,193
You are quite something, Mr. Rowdy!

1195
01:03:13,181 --> 01:03:15,248
You've got my whole village
under your spell!

1196
01:03:17,336 --> 01:03:18,821
Only the village is different...

1197
01:03:20,015 --> 01:03:21,737
Aren't the land and the people
just the same everywhere?

1198
01:03:22,246 --> 01:03:24,029
[Hopeful background music rises]

1199
01:03:25,837 --> 01:03:27,614
To me, Thomapuram and
Kaaniyaar aren't two,

1200
01:03:28,396 --> 01:03:29,402
but one!

1201
01:03:35,809 --> 01:03:37,761
[Hopeful background music fades]

1202
01:03:37,762 --> 01:03:38,972
This is the land I bought.

1203
01:03:40,295 --> 01:03:41,302
Do you like it?

1204
01:03:42,673 --> 01:03:45,395
This land by the banks of
the Amaravathi river was my dream.

1205
01:03:45,545 --> 01:03:48,229
I endured much
to finally call this land my own.

1206
01:03:51,909 --> 01:03:54,949
After all, the fight for land
is the same everywhere, isn't it?

1207
01:04:01,140 --> 01:04:03,467
Take Kurishumala, for instance.

1208
01:04:03,751 --> 01:04:06,095
The Party wants a
massive office there.

1209
01:04:07,869 --> 01:04:10,090
As for the church folk...
they want a brand new church.

1210
01:04:11,716 --> 01:04:12,941
But honestly,

1211
01:04:13,648 --> 01:04:15,437
is not a school
what is truly needed there?

1212
01:04:17,842 --> 01:04:23,568
Without having to struggle
through hills, ferries, rain, or floods,

1213
01:04:24,035 --> 01:04:29,560
the children here deserve
a school to study, do they not?

1214
01:04:30,194 --> 01:04:32,248
[Heartfelt background music]

1215
01:04:33,417 --> 01:04:35,390
How much land does this
property cover exactly?

1216
01:04:36,263 --> 01:04:38,535
It is roughly four or five acres
altogether.

1217
01:04:39,295 --> 01:04:41,962
Only six families have got title deeds
in Kunnumpuram.

1218
01:04:42,114 --> 01:04:43,334
Luckily, this is one of them.

1219
01:04:43,335 --> 01:04:45,133
And since it is deeded land,

1220
01:04:45,134 --> 01:04:46,762
a lot of people
have their eyes on it.

1221
01:04:48,102 --> 01:04:49,908
There are temptations,
threats, and the like.

1222
01:04:50,338 --> 01:04:51,635
Anyway, we will see.

1223
01:04:53,131 --> 01:04:55,243
Even after getting the land
you always wanted,

1224
01:04:55,244 --> 01:04:56,582
why have you not built a house?

1225
01:04:58,749 --> 01:05:01,195
I do not know if Kurishumala
will ever have a school.

1226
01:05:02,155 --> 01:05:03,472
But there will be one here,

1227
01:05:04,342 --> 01:05:05,349
right here on my soil.

1228
01:05:06,842 --> 01:05:08,989
That is now my greatest dream.

1229
01:05:10,528 --> 01:05:12,889
Isn't a small patch of land
enough for me to build a house?

1230
01:05:13,634 --> 01:05:15,361
[Hopeful background music rises]

1231
01:05:21,552 --> 01:05:23,062
[Hopeful background music fades]

1232
01:05:23,063 --> 01:05:25,055
I must leave tomorrow morning.

1233
01:05:25,854 --> 01:05:27,390
I have to reach Alappuzha by night.

1234
01:05:27,826 --> 01:05:29,264
- Shall I leave?
- Yes.

1235
01:05:35,136 --> 01:05:36,143
Hey?

1236
01:05:36,689 --> 01:05:37,696
Yes?

1237
01:05:38,909 --> 01:05:41,037
Didn't you ask me earlier
if I liked the play?

1238
01:05:43,388 --> 01:05:44,668
The play was excellent!

1239
01:05:46,057 --> 01:05:49,816
If the Christopher of Kaaniyaar
has liked our play,

1240
01:05:49,974 --> 01:05:52,283
it means that our play
will stand immortal.

1241
01:05:53,801 --> 01:05:55,841
[Background music rises]

1242
01:06:02,334 --> 01:06:04,733
[Background music fades]

1243
01:06:04,734 --> 01:06:06,314
[Lively village ambience]

1244
01:06:08,067 --> 01:06:10,233
What the hell
have you done, Christopher!

1245
01:06:10,234 --> 01:06:11,773
This was a bit too much!

1246
01:06:11,774 --> 01:06:13,342
- It was really bad!
- We trusted you!

1247
01:06:13,502 --> 01:06:14,502
He's a liar!

1248
01:06:14,766 --> 01:06:18,535
Here comes the "holy angel," hand-picked
by the Trustee and the young priest.

1249
01:06:19,102 --> 01:06:20,065
Look at that arrogance in his stride!

1250
01:06:20,066 --> 01:06:22,455
While KPAC staged
the play at Kurishumala...

1251
01:06:22,542 --> 01:06:25,912
was Christopher of Kunnumpuram
off fishing?

1252
01:06:25,913 --> 01:06:27,541
That was the question
from the Bishop House!

1253
01:06:27,542 --> 01:06:29,796
Oh! I felt flayed on the spot.

1254
01:06:29,926 --> 01:06:31,546
I knew this
from the very beginning!

1255
01:06:31,714 --> 01:06:33,327
Now tell me, Father,
are you satisfied?

1256
01:06:34,284 --> 01:06:35,868
The precious son you prayed for!

1257
01:06:35,869 --> 01:06:38,617
Oh, this 'precious son' wasn't
out catching fish at all.

1258
01:06:39,180 --> 01:06:41,242
There's that Communist
girl in Kunnumpuram, right?

1259
01:06:41,490 --> 01:06:42,762
K.P.A.C. Rebecca!

1260
01:06:42,996 --> 01:06:44,202
All of you, listen to this!

1261
01:06:44,429 --> 01:06:46,648
He was roaming
hand-in-hand with her!

1262
01:06:46,828 --> 01:06:48,502
I saw it with my own eyes, Father!

1263
01:06:49,854 --> 01:06:51,607
Listen, I'm telling
this to everyone here.

1264
01:06:51,836 --> 01:06:53,241
Just like he deceived you,

1265
01:06:53,242 --> 01:06:55,928
he blinded us too,
and went to support that play.

1266
01:06:56,661 --> 01:06:57,668
Did you see that play?

1267
01:06:59,090 --> 01:07:01,587
- Well, I saw it.
- Father, did you hear that?

1268
01:07:01,588 --> 01:07:02,588
Father!

1269
01:07:03,483 --> 01:07:06,125
The Communists performing that play,
don't have horns or tails.

1270
01:07:06,902 --> 01:07:09,022
They're just ordinary humans like us.

1271
01:07:09,462 --> 01:07:11,939
- Defending them after seeing it?
- How dare he talk like this?

1272
01:07:12,202 --> 01:07:13,389
- Just stay quiet.
- Oh, really!

1273
01:07:14,815 --> 01:07:15,887
My dear Father...

1274
01:07:15,888 --> 01:07:19,288
I did not see any of those so-called
Russian evil tactics in that play.

1275
01:07:20,954 --> 01:07:23,696
And we should not waste our time
discussing that play or the party.

1276
01:07:23,697 --> 01:07:26,092
We have far more to do
for the sake of Kaaniyaar.

1277
01:07:27,349 --> 01:07:29,260
In the play 'You Made Me a Communist',

1278
01:07:29,261 --> 01:07:32,971
there is no mention of Christians
or the Church, contrary to what you think.

1279
01:07:33,924 --> 01:07:35,424
That play is not against us, Father.

1280
01:07:39,470 --> 01:07:41,183
Are you even a Christian
to say that?

1281
01:07:41,269 --> 01:07:43,182
[Emotional background music begins]

1282
01:07:45,775 --> 01:07:47,175
Aren't you Krishna Pillai?

1283
01:07:48,974 --> 01:07:50,045
I'm asking you!

1284
01:07:50,417 --> 01:07:51,625
Aren't you Krishna Pillai?

1285
01:07:51,930 --> 01:07:52,937
Answer me!

1286
01:07:54,086 --> 01:07:55,653
[Emotional background music intensifies]

1287
01:07:56,835 --> 01:07:58,911
- Father...
- Get out of here right now!

1288
01:07:59,327 --> 01:08:00,745
For bearing all your expenses

1289
01:08:00,746 --> 01:08:03,152
and crowning you
as the Christopher of this land,

1290
01:08:03,342 --> 01:08:04,821
no matter how many times I confess,

1291
01:08:04,822 --> 01:08:06,317
the Almighty will never forgive me!

1292
01:08:06,664 --> 01:08:07,671
Vile sinner!

1293
01:08:09,978 --> 01:08:13,049
You have betrayed this church
and this entire village.

1294
01:08:13,050 --> 01:08:14,700
- Get out!
- Get lost, you scoundrel!

1295
01:08:14,943 --> 01:08:16,415
[Crowd clamoring]

1296
01:08:16,604 --> 01:08:18,690
Didn't you hear what Father said?
Get the hell out of here!

1297
01:08:18,691 --> 01:08:20,050
Kuncheria, kick him out right now!

1298
01:08:20,670 --> 01:08:22,485
- You heard what the Father said!
- Oh no! Aashaan!

1299
01:08:22,486 --> 01:08:23,510
Just go... get out!

1300
01:08:23,511 --> 01:08:25,872
- You went behind that girl, right?
- Never show your face here again!

1301
01:08:26,776 --> 01:08:27,887
- Get lost!
- Get out!

1302
01:08:33,618 --> 01:08:37,710
[Emotional background music rises]

1303
01:08:48,552 --> 01:08:52,825
Didn't you ask, Ayyanar Sir,
what makes this day so special?

1304
01:08:53,291 --> 01:08:54,291
Yes, sir.

1305
01:08:55,801 --> 01:08:56,939
Welcome, Sir.

1306
01:08:57,927 --> 01:08:59,899
This is our War Room!

1307
01:09:00,382 --> 01:09:02,302
[Sinister background music]

1308
01:09:04,565 --> 01:09:07,787
The great protest that shall enter
the annals of history tomorrow...

1309
01:09:08,587 --> 01:09:11,367
The Liberation Struggle.
This is its War Room.

1310
01:09:13,160 --> 01:09:17,445
For a long time now, my team and
I have been toiling day and night.

1311
01:09:17,629 --> 01:09:19,556
[Telephone rings]

1312
01:09:23,691 --> 01:09:24,691
Yes.

1313
01:09:26,301 --> 01:09:28,434
From this day forth,
the Liberation Struggle

1314
01:09:28,714 --> 01:09:30,164
surges towards its grand culmination,

1315
01:09:30,165 --> 01:09:31,462
[Church bell rings]
in Kaaniyaar!

1316
01:09:37,982 --> 01:09:40,168
[Powerful background music roars]

1317
01:09:42,147 --> 01:09:44,727
All of you, hear this well!

1318
01:09:45,013 --> 01:09:47,194
From today, the land of Kaaniyaar

1319
01:09:47,482 --> 01:09:50,152
shall have neither a Christopher
nor a Christopher Force!

1320
01:09:52,055 --> 01:09:56,604
No one needs to come here anymore
as the saviour of this land!

1321
01:09:56,715 --> 01:09:57,757
He will come, sir!

1322
01:09:57,758 --> 01:10:00,584
He is coming to set that land
ablaze until nothing but ash remains.

1323
01:10:01,023 --> 01:10:02,829
[Ominous music]

1324
01:10:05,288 --> 01:10:08,963
Over this holy sanctuary
blessed by the Almighty,

1325
01:10:08,964 --> 01:10:12,117
not even the shadow
of a devil shall fall.

1326
01:10:12,394 --> 01:10:14,361
[Dramatic background music rises]

1327
01:10:20,678 --> 01:10:23,918
The fabric of divine justice
will be torn asunder!

1328
01:10:25,248 --> 01:10:28,861
This land isn't
meant to be signed away

1329
01:10:29,158 --> 01:10:30,462
to any monopolist.

1330
01:10:30,562 --> 01:10:31,819
Tell them to leave!

1331
01:10:35,073 --> 01:10:36,512
[Laughs loudly]

1332
01:10:37,255 --> 01:10:39,314
The great serpent of doom

1333
01:10:39,632 --> 01:10:41,399
will descend on Earth!

1334
01:10:43,859 --> 01:10:47,257
To sever this land's veins
one by one, until they snap...

1335
01:10:47,464 --> 01:10:48,775
he is coming...

1336
01:10:48,776 --> 01:10:50,616
[Ominous background music swells]

1337
01:10:51,225 --> 01:10:52,949
The massacre specialist...

1338
01:10:55,495 --> 01:10:56,848
Rairu Ramanna!

1339
01:10:59,475 --> 01:11:00,475
Yes.

1340
01:11:00,748 --> 01:11:01,748
He is coming...

1341
01:11:02,055 --> 01:11:03,328
for Kaaniyaar.

1342
01:11:06,853 --> 01:11:08,993
[Ominous background music rises]

1343
01:11:19,530 --> 01:11:21,749
[Ominous background music fades]

1344
01:11:21,750 --> 01:11:22,824
[Birds chirping]

1345
01:11:22,963 --> 01:11:25,956
Hey, I heard the church bells ringing
again this morning.

1346
01:11:26,108 --> 01:11:27,415
What was it about?

1347
01:11:27,416 --> 01:11:30,403
I don't know.
Chachan and Paappan have gone there.

1348
01:11:30,509 --> 01:11:31,748
Lonappan Chettayi!

1349
01:11:31,862 --> 01:11:33,062
- Chettayi!
- Yes?

1350
01:11:33,655 --> 01:11:36,325
Beyond Kunnumpuram is Thariyottumala Hill.
We must not go there.

1351
01:11:36,326 --> 01:11:39,452
Kuttayi, there is really good honey there.
Do you want to come along?

1352
01:11:39,609 --> 01:11:41,828
I'm not coming.
Chettayi told us not to go there.

1353
01:11:41,829 --> 01:11:44,089
Listen, there are no demons there
in the daytime.

1354
01:11:44,796 --> 01:11:45,734
Come, let's go.

1355
01:11:45,735 --> 01:11:47,929
- Hey Johnny, then shall we go too?
- Yes.

1356
01:11:51,612 --> 01:11:53,405
Lonappan Chettayi,
we are coming along too!

1357
01:11:53,614 --> 01:11:54,720
Alright, come along.

1358
01:11:54,878 --> 01:11:58,378
But do not tell anyone
we went to Thariyottumala Hill.

1359
01:11:58,478 --> 01:12:01,857
[Ominous music]

1360
01:12:04,033 --> 01:12:06,692
Do you get it now?
This was utterly pointless!

1361
01:12:07,064 --> 01:12:09,682
Instead of remaining in our own land,
minding our own affairs...

1362
01:12:11,198 --> 01:12:12,881
Tell me, what was wrong
with this Father Gregory?

1363
01:12:12,882 --> 01:12:14,288
That is what I cannot understand.

1364
01:12:14,501 --> 01:12:17,635
We were living peacefully, staging
our plays and picking our fights,

1365
01:12:17,818 --> 01:12:20,098
and they dragged us here
to listen to all their accusations!

1366
01:12:20,099 --> 01:12:21,567
It was all in vain.

1367
01:12:23,176 --> 01:12:24,395
Forget it, Saali!

1368
01:12:25,463 --> 01:12:27,510
Once you decide to end everything
and walk away...

1369
01:12:27,736 --> 01:12:28,792
that is the end of it.

1370
01:12:29,132 --> 01:12:30,254
You have to let it go.

1371
01:12:35,182 --> 01:12:36,422
[Emotional background music]

1372
01:12:36,423 --> 01:12:37,995
If there is anything worth remembering,

1373
01:12:38,717 --> 01:12:40,163
only that should be carried with us.

1374
01:12:40,628 --> 01:12:42,628
[Emotional background music continues]

1375
01:12:43,771 --> 01:12:44,871
Huh?

1376
01:12:45,944 --> 01:12:46,957
Aashaan!

1377
01:12:49,929 --> 01:12:51,929
[Background music intensifies]

1378
01:12:56,688 --> 01:12:58,688
[Intense music]

1379
01:13:03,471 --> 01:13:05,471
[Music continues]

1380
01:13:09,024 --> 01:13:10,378
Don't go, Aashaan!

1381
01:13:10,945 --> 01:13:13,318
No matter what the Church says,
you must not leave, Aashaan!

1382
01:13:13,319 --> 01:13:16,316
They are saying
they will disband the Christopher Force.

1383
01:13:16,317 --> 01:13:17,339
If you leave,

1384
01:13:17,766 --> 01:13:19,091
we will come with you, Aashaan!

1385
01:13:21,477 --> 01:13:22,543
I must go.

1386
01:13:23,156 --> 01:13:24,177
I have to.

1387
01:13:28,234 --> 01:13:29,577
- Aashaan...
- Bye.

1388
01:13:29,986 --> 01:13:32,803
- Aashaan! Don't go, Aashaan.
- Christopher Aashaan!

1389
01:13:37,530 --> 01:13:39,802
Krishna Pillai and Pothan Christopher
are not two,

1390
01:13:40,020 --> 01:13:41,023
but one...

1391
01:13:41,363 --> 01:13:42,982
and you must proclaim it
to this land.

1392
01:13:43,106 --> 01:13:45,106
[Background music soars]

1393
01:13:54,882 --> 01:13:57,512
[Background music fades]

1394
01:13:57,513 --> 01:13:59,350
Hey! Christopher Krishna Pillai!

1395
01:14:01,987 --> 01:14:04,900
When the church bell tolled this
morning, I had guessed it already.

1396
01:14:06,603 --> 01:14:10,032
Too bad I wasn't there to watch
the adopted son being shown the door.

1397
01:14:10,255 --> 01:14:13,027
No one has cast us out.
We are leaving of our own accord.

1398
01:14:13,370 --> 01:14:14,383
Hmm.

1399
01:14:14,534 --> 01:14:15,554
Yes, I know.

1400
01:14:17,048 --> 01:14:19,211
Then why are your Aashaan's
eyes filled with tears?

1401
01:14:19,212 --> 01:14:21,557
What? Nothing like that.
His eyes are just sweating.

1402
01:14:21,558 --> 01:14:23,268
Aashaan has a slight
sweating problem!

1403
01:14:23,269 --> 01:14:24,939
What a master,
and what a disciple.

1404
01:14:24,940 --> 01:14:26,422
- Comrade!
- Yes?

1405
01:14:26,423 --> 01:14:27,450
Are you leaving?

1406
01:14:27,951 --> 01:14:30,799
I must reach Alappuzha by noon.
There is a play this evening.

1407
01:14:30,800 --> 01:14:33,153
Then you should have caught
the six-thirty bus!

1408
01:14:33,154 --> 01:14:34,867
The next bus will be quite late.

1409
01:14:35,126 --> 01:14:36,468
Is that so? Ugh!

1410
01:14:36,469 --> 01:14:37,575
Anyway, never mind.

1411
01:14:47,843 --> 01:14:49,317
Comrade, shall I leave?

1412
01:14:50,950 --> 01:14:52,018
Okay then.

1413
01:14:52,264 --> 01:14:54,264
[Soft music]

1414
01:14:55,262 --> 01:14:56,895
Next stop is at Memala, right?

1415
01:14:58,802 --> 01:15:00,802
[Bus approaching]

1416
01:15:03,682 --> 01:15:04,922
[Bus bell rings]

1417
01:15:06,109 --> 01:15:07,254
See you.

1418
01:15:07,424 --> 01:15:09,424
[Background music rises]

1419
01:15:14,121 --> 01:15:15,160
[Bus bell ringing]

1420
01:15:16,293 --> 01:15:17,293
[Bus bell ringing]

1421
01:15:22,007 --> 01:15:24,007
[Music continues]

1422
01:15:30,857 --> 01:15:32,857
[Bangles jingling]

1423
01:15:38,444 --> 01:15:40,444
[Laughs]

1424
01:15:41,089 --> 01:15:42,585
My dear rowdy!

1425
01:15:43,378 --> 01:15:44,605
Can't you smile a little?

1426
01:15:46,569 --> 01:15:47,793
Wait… so,

1427
01:15:47,794 --> 01:15:49,267
aren't you going to Alappuzha?

1428
01:15:50,694 --> 01:15:52,894
I can take a bus
from Ayyathankovil as well.

1429
01:15:52,895 --> 01:15:54,255
[Soft music]

1430
01:15:55,286 --> 01:15:57,286
[Both laugh]

1431
01:15:59,093 --> 01:16:01,093
[Song begins]

1432
01:16:03,848 --> 01:16:07,213
♪ Never till this day
have I seen ♪

1433
01:16:09,467 --> 01:16:12,627
♪ A maiden's face
in molten gold's sheen ♪

1434
01:16:14,939 --> 01:16:17,612
♪ Never till this day
have I seen ♪

1435
01:16:17,766 --> 01:16:20,478
♪ A maiden's face
in molten gold's sheen ♪

1436
01:16:20,479 --> 01:16:23,369
♪ Descended from heaven
to join me on earth ♪

1437
01:16:23,370 --> 01:16:25,857
♪ This maiden so precious,
of boundless worth ♪

1438
01:16:26,049 --> 01:16:28,860
♪ A moonlight found
after a patient search ♪

1439
01:16:28,861 --> 01:16:31,582
♪ Like golden rain that fell
at midnight's verge ♪

1440
01:16:31,583 --> 01:16:36,843
♪ A tender alphabet, fine and rare,
Penned by a feather-tip with care ♪

1441
01:16:37,165 --> 01:16:42,539
♪ The first light that springs
from a limitless sunrise ♪

1442
01:16:42,745 --> 01:16:47,762
♪ A golden sky shimmering
wide in my eyes ♪

1443
01:16:47,763 --> 01:16:51,020
♪ In the corner of dreams
where it gently would reign ♪

1444
01:16:51,021 --> 01:16:53,094
♪ Like a tender bloom
kissed by cooling rain ♪

1445
01:16:53,755 --> 01:16:56,553
♪ Let the wild magnolia bloom ♪

1446
01:16:56,554 --> 01:16:59,300
♪ Let the parrot hear it ring
across the gloom ♪

1447
01:16:59,301 --> 01:17:04,781
♪ You are the maiden meant for me,
my only destiny ♪

1448
01:17:04,877 --> 01:17:07,645
♪ You are the pearl I found
after waiting for years ♪

1449
01:17:07,646 --> 01:17:10,423
♪ You are the gold I found
after searching all spheres ♪

1450
01:17:10,424 --> 01:17:14,836
♪ The treasure of desire I stole,
beyond all my fears ♪

1451
01:17:38,015 --> 01:17:43,151
♪ Will you come?
Will you come this way, my dear? ♪

1452
01:17:43,152 --> 01:17:48,395
♪ My feet are weary waiting for you,
my gentle deer ♪

1453
01:17:48,656 --> 01:17:53,870
♪ Do not go, do not go,
do not let go of my hand ♪

1454
01:17:53,969 --> 01:18:00,198
♪ When a hundred yearnings
and desires take command ♪

1455
01:18:00,199 --> 01:18:05,751
♪ A romantic exchange
between the shore and the wave ♪

1456
01:18:05,752 --> 01:18:11,143
♪ A soft serenade
the wind through bamboo would weave ♪

1457
01:18:11,144 --> 01:18:15,297
♪ O morning when the cloud-arrayed sky,
lets gentle rain fall from on high ♪

1458
01:18:16,858 --> 01:18:19,656
♪ Let the wild magnolia bloom ♪

1459
01:18:19,657 --> 01:18:22,403
♪ Let the parrot hear it ring
across the gloom ♪

1460
01:18:22,404 --> 01:18:27,932
♪ You are the maiden meant for me,
my only destiny ♪

1461
01:18:27,933 --> 01:18:30,719
♪ You are the pearl I found
after waiting for years ♪

1462
01:18:30,720 --> 01:18:33,506
♪ You are the gold I found
after searching all spheres ♪

1463
01:18:34,933 --> 01:18:36,886
No more farewells.
I'll see you then.

1464
01:18:37,767 --> 01:18:38,830
Okay.

1465
01:18:49,954 --> 01:18:51,447
[Heartwarming background music rises]

1466
01:18:59,814 --> 01:19:02,032
Ticket!
Ticket! Where are you headed, Chetta?

1467
01:19:03,669 --> 01:19:04,689
Ticket! Ticket!

1468
01:19:05,112 --> 01:19:08,689
[Communist Manifesto] To Comrade
Krishna Pillai, with love, Rebecca!

1469
01:19:08,690 --> 01:19:10,690
[Romantic music]

1470
01:19:13,529 --> 01:19:15,529
[Music swells]

1471
01:19:17,226 --> 01:19:18,232
Hey!

1472
01:19:24,083 --> 01:19:25,270
[Bus bell rings]

1473
01:19:27,389 --> 01:19:28,946
[Laughs]

1474
01:19:30,015 --> 01:19:31,142
Comrade!

1475
01:19:32,000 --> 01:19:33,147
What did you just call me?

1476
01:19:33,909 --> 01:19:34,973
He called you Comrade!

1477
01:19:38,115 --> 01:19:41,133
You have only seen Keramane Shivarama
Hegde's Ravana Charitham, haven't you?

1478
01:19:41,842 --> 01:19:42,914
- Yes!
- Now...

1479
01:19:43,477 --> 01:19:44,628
at Thommapuram...

1480
01:19:45,289 --> 01:19:46,327
will you come

1481
01:19:46,935 --> 01:19:49,736
to watch the Ravana Charitham
performed by me, Krishna Pillai?

1482
01:19:51,275 --> 01:19:52,361
I will.

1483
01:19:54,328 --> 01:19:56,328
[Heartwarming background music
continues]

1484
01:20:15,988 --> 01:20:17,988
[Heartwarming background music fades]

1485
01:20:22,107 --> 01:20:24,107
[Machine whirring]

1486
01:20:28,839 --> 01:20:30,559
[Telephone rings]

1487
01:20:30,645 --> 01:20:31,645
Sir!

1488
01:20:31,885 --> 01:20:33,885
I just got the report, Sir.
Yes, Sir.

1489
01:20:34,392 --> 01:20:36,942
Evening, 4:30.
I will inform, Sir.

1490
01:20:37,240 --> 01:20:38,632
[Tense music]

1491
01:20:40,559 --> 01:20:42,559
[Typing]

1492
01:20:45,719 --> 01:20:46,868
No, not now.

1493
01:20:48,493 --> 01:20:49,509
CM...

1494
01:20:49,841 --> 01:20:51,259
there's an important message, sir.

1495
01:20:52,540 --> 01:20:53,584
Sir!

1496
01:20:53,585 --> 01:20:55,585
[Tense music]

1497
01:21:01,579 --> 01:21:03,579
[Bus comes to a stop]

1498
01:21:06,614 --> 01:21:07,707
Why did you stop, Ramettan?

1499
01:21:08,034 --> 01:21:09,450
Someone is blocking the way.

1500
01:21:09,451 --> 01:21:10,923
[Tense music rises]

1501
01:21:13,023 --> 01:21:14,867
[Ominous music]

1502
01:21:17,098 --> 01:21:18,106
Who is he?

1503
01:21:20,943 --> 01:21:22,943
[Music intensifies]

1504
01:21:26,178 --> 01:21:27,361
Hey!

1505
01:21:27,362 --> 01:21:28,975
What are you doing?

1506
01:21:32,622 --> 01:21:33,822
Move your bike!

1507
01:21:34,888 --> 01:21:36,048
What are you doing?

1508
01:21:36,861 --> 01:21:37,901
- Give it back!
- Sorry!

1509
01:21:38,225 --> 01:21:40,042
Hey! What do you think
you are doing?

1510
01:21:41,638 --> 01:21:42,795
You better behave yourself!

1511
01:21:42,796 --> 01:21:45,135
- Hey, move your bike!
- How dare you lay your hands on a woman?

1512
01:21:45,136 --> 01:21:48,138
- Is he deaf or something?
- Conductor, throw him out!

1513
01:21:48,852 --> 01:21:51,476
- Get out of the bus!
- I've been telling him the same, Sister.

1514
01:21:51,477 --> 01:21:53,574
- I'm talking to you!
- Look, the locals will make a scene!

1515
01:21:53,575 --> 01:21:54,750
- Can't you understa--
- Oh no!

1516
01:21:56,169 --> 01:21:57,462
[In Telugu] I don't say goodbyes.

1517
01:21:57,875 --> 01:21:59,282
- Sorry!
- [Gunshot]

1518
01:22:04,212 --> 01:22:06,176
[People shouting]

1519
01:22:06,177 --> 01:22:07,724
[Emotional music]

1520
01:22:12,078 --> 01:22:13,224
[Laughs]

1521
01:22:14,434 --> 01:22:15,493
[Gunfire]

1522
01:22:18,030 --> 01:22:20,030
[Music continues]

1523
01:22:27,568 --> 01:22:29,568
[Boots approaching]

1524
01:22:30,501 --> 01:22:33,007
[Grave, dramatic music]

1525
01:22:35,550 --> 01:22:37,610
I came here for you alone.

1526
01:22:38,547 --> 01:22:39,633
What to do!

1527
01:22:40,394 --> 01:22:41,556
Collateral damage.

1528
01:22:43,049 --> 01:22:44,469
[Gunshot]

1529
01:22:46,443 --> 01:22:48,915
Sir, as part of the Liberation Struggle,

1530
01:22:49,234 --> 01:22:51,610
a bomb attack was carried out
on a bus in Muvattupuzha.

1531
01:22:52,551 --> 01:22:54,496
[Intense music]

1532
01:22:54,497 --> 01:22:55,824
[Screams]

1533
01:22:58,877 --> 01:22:59,979
Aashaan!

1534
01:23:00,088 --> 01:23:02,088
[Explosion]

1535
01:23:02,373 --> 01:23:03,659
[Body falls]

1536
01:23:03,906 --> 01:23:05,046
Aashaan!

1537
01:23:05,365 --> 01:23:06,992
Aashaan! Get up!

1538
01:23:09,577 --> 01:23:11,243
Come dear, don't be scared.

1539
01:23:12,536 --> 01:23:13,702
Get the jeep!

1540
01:23:13,892 --> 01:23:15,205
[Swearing in another language]

1541
01:23:15,645 --> 01:23:16,646
Aashaan!

1542
01:23:16,918 --> 01:23:18,203
Aashaan, get in.

1543
01:23:18,809 --> 01:23:19,701
Come!

1544
01:23:19,702 --> 01:23:20,993
[in unknown language]
Hey, come on!

1545
01:23:20,994 --> 01:23:22,620
- Aashaan!
- Let's go!

1546
01:23:22,621 --> 01:23:23,734
Get in quickly!

1547
01:23:25,023 --> 01:23:26,175
Watch your step... Get in!

1548
01:23:27,123 --> 01:23:28,483
Is there a hospital nearby?

1549
01:23:29,617 --> 01:23:30,959
Who are these people?

1550
01:23:30,960 --> 01:23:32,960
[Mysterious theme]

1551
01:23:36,604 --> 01:23:37,632
Okay, okay.

1552
01:23:39,485 --> 01:23:40,496
CM...

1553
01:23:40,986 --> 01:23:43,848
The police fired four rounds
at the protesters in Piravom.

1554
01:23:44,604 --> 01:23:45,481
FIRE!!

1555
01:23:45,482 --> 01:23:46,742
[Gunshot]

1556
01:23:47,524 --> 01:23:48,611
[Screams]

1557
01:23:49,563 --> 01:23:54,161
Sir, seven people, including a pregnant
woman, were killed on the spot.

1558
01:23:55,532 --> 01:23:59,530
Have goons now infiltrated
the police force?

1559
01:23:59,799 --> 01:24:00,799
Sir...

1560
01:24:01,414 --> 01:24:02,414
[Gunfire]

1561
01:24:03,633 --> 01:24:04,705
[Glass shatters]

1562
01:24:04,870 --> 01:24:06,753
[Radio] The Liberation Struggle
has erupted into street warfare!

1563
01:24:07,610 --> 01:24:09,492
Central Kerala has become
a field of carnage.

1564
01:24:09,945 --> 01:24:12,885
Two people have been killed in
a police firing at Ambalapuzha.

1565
01:24:13,284 --> 01:24:15,284
[Jeep approaches]

1566
01:24:17,399 --> 01:24:19,399
- Stop.. Stop!
- Saali! Get out, quickly!

1567
01:24:20,230 --> 01:24:22,030
- Come!
- Watch your step, come!

1568
01:24:22,536 --> 01:24:23,635
Come on!

1569
01:24:23,789 --> 01:24:24,856
Ah.. come in.

1570
01:24:24,942 --> 01:24:26,699
- Go!
- Step aside!

1571
01:24:27,996 --> 01:24:29,334
- Mom!
- What is it?

1572
01:24:29,480 --> 01:24:30,789
Mom!

1573
01:24:31,280 --> 01:24:32,907
Mom!

1574
01:24:33,684 --> 01:24:34,913
Mom!

1575
01:24:34,914 --> 01:24:37,621
- Don't cry, dear.
- Chechi.. Chechi, my daughter!

1576
01:24:37,815 --> 01:24:38,980
Chinnu, my child!

1577
01:24:39,755 --> 01:24:40,763
Oh, no!

1578
01:24:41,302 --> 01:24:42,667
Dear, your mother is here.

1579
01:24:44,445 --> 01:24:45,944
Don't cry, dear.

1580
01:24:57,734 --> 01:24:59,734
[Thunder rumbles]

1581
01:25:03,197 --> 01:25:05,197
[Crying]

1582
01:25:05,639 --> 01:25:07,639
[Rain falling]

1583
01:25:12,242 --> 01:25:13,562
[Crying]

1584
01:25:20,517 --> 01:25:22,264
[Background music rises]

1585
01:25:36,123 --> 01:25:38,123
[Heartbreaking background music rises]

1586
01:25:44,976 --> 01:25:46,976
[Somber background music]

1587
01:25:59,607 --> 01:26:01,607
[Melancholy theme]

1588
01:26:12,628 --> 01:26:14,628
[Thunder rumbles]

1589
01:26:19,433 --> 01:26:21,433
[Soft music]

1590
01:26:27,116 --> 01:26:29,116
[Rain falling]

1591
01:26:29,326 --> 01:26:31,326
[Thunder rumbles]

1592
01:26:31,825 --> 01:26:33,386
Comrade, this is the man.

1593
01:26:34,865 --> 01:26:37,201
- This is the conductor of the Jupiter bus.
- Oh!

1594
01:26:37,671 --> 01:26:39,024
I ran and managed to escape.

1595
01:26:39,481 --> 01:26:41,979
A man boarded the bus alone
and began firing continuously.

1596
01:26:42,513 --> 01:26:44,771
He spoke a different language.

1597
01:26:44,945 --> 01:26:47,472
From his attire,
I doubt he was a protester.

1598
01:26:47,473 --> 01:26:49,819
[Swearing in another language]

1599
01:26:50,766 --> 01:26:52,790
[Tense music]

1600
01:26:52,791 --> 01:26:53,796
Rathnakaran, this...

1601
01:26:53,797 --> 01:26:56,087
Comrade, what is going on here?

1602
01:26:58,684 --> 01:27:00,597
[Radio] The Liberation Struggle
is turning

1603
01:27:00,598 --> 01:27:02,534
increasingly violent
across the entire state.

1604
01:27:02,904 --> 01:27:06,378
Four people were killed in the
police firings at Pulluvila and Vettukaadu.

1605
01:27:06,379 --> 01:27:08,901
CM, the situation is slipping
out of our control.

1606
01:27:09,625 --> 01:27:11,891
The rebellion is spreading
across the entire state.

1607
01:27:12,803 --> 01:27:15,850
A letter recommending the dismissal
of the state government

1608
01:27:15,851 --> 01:27:18,024
has been submitted by the IB
to the Prime Minister.

1609
01:27:18,025 --> 01:27:20,589
If the Governor sends his report as well...

1610
01:27:20,799 --> 01:27:21,982
Our government?

1611
01:27:24,288 --> 01:27:25,808
Losing power

1612
01:27:26,522 --> 01:27:28,465
is of no concern to me.

1613
01:27:29,327 --> 01:27:31,312
But what of my people?

1614
01:27:32,116 --> 01:27:33,234
Their tears,

1615
01:27:33,721 --> 01:27:35,521
the blood they have shed...

1616
01:27:35,988 --> 01:27:37,161
I'm sure,

1617
01:27:37,420 --> 01:27:39,492
someone is behind all this.

1618
01:27:39,625 --> 01:27:41,625
[Surging music]

1619
01:27:44,430 --> 01:27:48,537
A project already approved by the
Central Government… the Kaaniyaar project.

1620
01:27:50,151 --> 01:27:53,921
For it to take off, all that remained
was the State Government's clearance.

1621
01:27:53,922 --> 01:27:55,395
[Mysterious music]

1622
01:27:57,563 --> 01:28:00,116
But then came
the Communist Chief Minister's order.

1623
01:28:03,881 --> 01:28:05,234
Proposal rejected!

1624
01:28:05,235 --> 01:28:06,574
[C.M.] Tell them to leave!

1625
01:28:06,699 --> 01:28:09,725
So then, what do you think the man
who spent a fortune on this will do now?

1626
01:28:11,647 --> 01:28:12,599
Sir...

1627
01:28:12,600 --> 01:28:13,980
He would not heed us, sir.

1628
01:28:15,499 --> 01:28:17,467
We placed every possible
offer before him, sir.

1629
01:28:17,776 --> 01:28:20,376
But CM rejected them.

1630
01:28:20,377 --> 01:28:22,377
[Dog barking]

1631
01:28:30,220 --> 01:28:32,675
If it was the State Government
that stood in his way,

1632
01:28:32,949 --> 01:28:36,799
he resolved to bring down that
very government and reclaim that land.

1633
01:28:36,800 --> 01:28:38,800
[Dog continues barking]

1634
01:28:39,455 --> 01:28:41,661
The rightful sovereign of that land!

1635
01:28:47,132 --> 01:28:48,399
The great...

1636
01:28:48,400 --> 01:28:50,215
Pattelar Kunjambu Nambiar!

1637
01:28:50,216 --> 01:28:55,355
[Fierce rhythmic score]

1638
01:29:00,514 --> 01:29:02,427
[Majestic music]

1639
01:29:08,104 --> 01:29:10,309
There is but one punishment
for disobedience.

1640
01:29:11,393 --> 01:29:13,119
[Fierce rhythmic score]

1641
01:29:15,022 --> 01:29:16,486
Whichever dog it may be!

1642
01:29:21,235 --> 01:29:24,189
Thirty years ago,
to the Madikeri Palace,

1643
01:29:24,743 --> 01:29:28,223
he summoned those who coveted
this very land of Kaaniyaar…

1644
01:29:28,615 --> 01:29:29,894
and annihilated them.

1645
01:29:30,108 --> 01:29:31,514
The lone tusker.

1646
01:29:38,512 --> 01:29:40,810
The response to the
letter you sent...

1647
01:29:43,242 --> 01:29:45,894
you will find it inside the grain chest
in which you'll be buried.

1648
01:29:46,697 --> 01:29:47,715
[Gunshot]

1649
01:29:49,574 --> 01:29:51,574
[Horse neighs]

1650
01:29:55,746 --> 01:29:56,966
[Gunshot]

1651
01:29:57,324 --> 01:29:59,747
[Ferocious battle music]

1652
01:29:59,748 --> 01:30:01,614
[Horse neighs]

1653
01:30:04,362 --> 01:30:06,362
[Pulsing music]

1654
01:30:10,123 --> 01:30:12,123
[Intense music]

1655
01:30:18,703 --> 01:30:19,617
[Flesh impact]

1656
01:30:19,750 --> 01:30:23,587
Even as he spread fear and brought
the whole world beneath his feet,

1657
01:30:24,024 --> 01:30:27,235
there remained but one thing
that would not yield to him.

1658
01:30:28,503 --> 01:30:29,976
His ancestral land.

1659
01:30:34,273 --> 01:30:38,010
A hill no greater than a mustard seed
on the map of Kerala.

1660
01:30:39,066 --> 01:30:41,632
By making people believe
it was haunted by spirits and demons,

1661
01:30:41,759 --> 01:30:43,244
all these years,

1662
01:30:43,245 --> 01:30:46,576
he did not allow
even a hawk to fly above it…

1663
01:30:46,685 --> 01:30:50,123
The Devil's Hill of Kaaniyaar,
which he had long guarded.

1664
01:30:55,348 --> 01:30:56,854
There's something here.

1665
01:30:57,220 --> 01:30:59,214
- What is it?
- Chettayi, look!

1666
01:31:03,669 --> 01:31:04,857
Hey, come on!

1667
01:31:07,941 --> 01:31:09,521
What happened, Chettayi?

1668
01:31:09,702 --> 01:31:11,133
Something struck my leg.

1669
01:31:13,526 --> 01:31:15,102
That's Thariyottumala Hill.

1670
01:31:17,275 --> 01:31:18,716
That's the land of demons.

1671
01:31:19,824 --> 01:31:20,826
Hey!

1672
01:31:21,321 --> 01:31:22,525
Run!

1673
01:31:22,526 --> 01:31:24,007
- Oh my God!
- Run!

1674
01:31:24,008 --> 01:31:26,467
Within that ravine of Kaaniyaar,

1675
01:31:26,581 --> 01:31:28,816
where he slaughtered all
who coveted it…

1676
01:31:28,950 --> 01:31:30,774
Do you know what lies there,
Ayyanar sir?

1677
01:31:32,365 --> 01:31:33,594
Gold!

1678
01:31:35,201 --> 01:31:38,982
An entire mountain of gold,
ready to be mined.

1679
01:31:40,317 --> 01:31:41,408
Thariyottumala Hill.

1680
01:31:41,734 --> 01:31:43,094
[Thunder rumbles]

1681
01:31:45,090 --> 01:31:47,090
In the name of the Malabar Mining Company,

1682
01:31:47,337 --> 01:31:51,776
all that he had amassed from
across the world over all these years…

1683
01:31:51,777 --> 01:31:54,499
He realised all of it amounted
to nothing in comparison.

1684
01:31:55,144 --> 01:31:57,641
Because in a single ravine
of Kaaniyaar,

1685
01:31:57,642 --> 01:32:01,234
there lay riches tenfold greater
than all he had acquired.

1686
01:32:02,007 --> 01:32:04,574
For that,
he set his plans in motion.

1687
01:32:04,737 --> 01:32:08,126
Chests of money, bearing the seal
of the Malabar Mining Company

1688
01:32:08,709 --> 01:32:10,562
were distributed in abundance

1689
01:32:10,735 --> 01:32:15,083
to protesters, politicians,
journalists, and religious leaders,

1690
01:32:15,194 --> 01:32:17,608
from Indraprastha to Ananthapuri.

1691
01:32:18,165 --> 01:32:21,041
Then came the decision
of the Communist Chief Minister.

1692
01:32:21,309 --> 01:32:22,604
Project rejected!

1693
01:32:23,315 --> 01:32:27,251
That day, he pronounced the end
of the Communist government.

1694
01:32:27,626 --> 01:32:30,779
Rairu, in three days from now,

1695
01:32:31,204 --> 01:32:33,863
the Kerala Government
must face its end.

1696
01:32:35,224 --> 01:32:36,311
Okay, Sir.

1697
01:32:38,916 --> 01:32:41,648
By means of my influence
within the Home Department,

1698
01:32:41,893 --> 01:32:45,398
I had Rairu appointed
as Special Task Officer for Kaaniyaar

1699
01:32:45,484 --> 01:32:47,188
by the Inspector General.

1700
01:32:51,376 --> 01:32:52,423
[Gunshot]

1701
01:32:52,424 --> 01:32:54,104
[Dramatic music rises]

1702
01:32:54,682 --> 01:32:57,406
Among the Liberation Struggle agitators
and within the police force,

1703
01:32:57,827 --> 01:32:59,844
I planted Rairu's men,

1704
01:33:00,091 --> 01:33:03,851
and undertook the task
of bringing down this government.

1705
01:33:05,750 --> 01:33:07,750
[Intense background music]

1706
01:33:09,156 --> 01:33:11,365
Then… to reclaim that land,

1707
01:33:11,719 --> 01:33:13,993
there was Special Officer
Rairu Ramanna…

1708
01:33:14,891 --> 01:33:16,710
And the impediment
that stood in the way,

1709
01:33:17,381 --> 01:33:19,004
was that sixth title deed.

1710
01:33:20,533 --> 01:33:22,839
[Ominous background music]

1711
01:33:25,018 --> 01:33:27,504
Hey! What do you think
you are doing?

1712
01:33:30,112 --> 01:33:31,252
[Gunshot]

1713
01:33:32,685 --> 01:33:34,129
[Mournful music]

1714
01:33:40,218 --> 01:33:42,218
[Music continues]

1715
01:33:47,413 --> 01:33:52,108
This land by the banks of
the Amaravathi river was my dream.

1716
01:33:53,036 --> 01:33:54,496
Since it is deeded land,

1717
01:33:54,497 --> 01:33:56,041
a lot of people
have their eyes on it.

1718
01:33:56,292 --> 01:33:58,292
There are temptations,
threats, and the like.

1719
01:34:01,751 --> 01:34:03,291
[Music builds]

1720
01:34:03,292 --> 01:34:05,311
Under the pretext
of the Liberation Struggle,

1721
01:34:05,557 --> 01:34:08,888
by tomorrow at daybreak,
this government will be brought down.

1722
01:34:09,367 --> 01:34:10,691
But that is not all.

1723
01:34:10,832 --> 01:34:12,658
Under the cover of this struggle…

1724
01:34:12,783 --> 01:34:15,258
the village of Kaaniyaar,
which stood as an impediment

1725
01:34:15,525 --> 01:34:18,585
between Pattelar Saab
and Thariyottumala Hill,

1726
01:34:19,114 --> 01:34:22,129
will be wiped off
the map of Kerala itself.

1727
01:34:22,623 --> 01:34:23,977
[Church bell tolls]

1728
01:34:27,293 --> 01:34:28,313
[Thunder rumbles]

1729
01:34:28,740 --> 01:34:31,843
[Church bells ringing]

1730
01:34:31,844 --> 01:34:33,844
[Loud thunder]

1731
01:34:34,990 --> 01:34:36,990
[Church bells continue]

1732
01:34:42,612 --> 01:34:43,996
[Bells continue ringing]

1733
01:34:43,997 --> 01:34:45,450
Who is it at this hour, Father?

1734
01:34:48,045 --> 01:34:50,045
[Lightning crashes]

1735
01:34:50,978 --> 01:34:51,718
[Police Station, Ayyathan Kovil]

1736
01:34:51,719 --> 01:34:54,104
Didn't you see everything, sir?
They weren't pelting stones.

1737
01:34:54,314 --> 01:34:55,975
The police picked them up
by mistake.

1738
01:34:56,317 --> 01:34:58,728
Listen, my head is already aching
from all this.

1739
01:34:59,593 --> 01:35:01,416
Enough of your stories.
Step aside!

1740
01:35:01,815 --> 01:35:02,815
Shucks!

1741
01:35:03,147 --> 01:35:06,041
- Listen, you all stay here.
- We don't have time, Kunjoonju.

1742
01:35:06,042 --> 01:35:08,113
Get the cycle and reach
the Taluk hospital at once.

1743
01:35:10,437 --> 01:35:15,143
Cut all power and phone lines to
the Kaaniyaar division immediately.

1744
01:35:15,396 --> 01:35:17,449
And set up full surveillance to ensure

1745
01:35:17,450 --> 01:35:20,349
no other boats can reach
the Kunnumpuram side.

1746
01:35:20,970 --> 01:35:22,096
[Sinister background music]

1747
01:35:22,097 --> 01:35:23,830
Kaaniyaar's Kunnumpuram.

1748
01:35:24,380 --> 01:35:28,170
This is the only entry point
to Thariyottumala Hill.

1749
01:35:28,927 --> 01:35:30,864
[Background music intensifies]

1750
01:35:30,865 --> 01:35:33,738
Without any title deeds,
a swarm of wretched parasites

1751
01:35:34,052 --> 01:35:35,795
has bred and multiplied here,

1752
01:35:36,053 --> 01:35:38,186
blocking our path
and clinging on.

1753
01:35:38,787 --> 01:35:41,677
The final revolt
of the Liberation Struggle

1754
01:35:42,343 --> 01:35:44,481
will unfold in Kaaniyaar
tonight.

1755
01:35:44,874 --> 01:35:47,010
Eight or ten deaths
will not suffice!

1756
01:35:48,170 --> 01:35:49,343
Kunnumpuram...

1757
01:35:50,065 --> 01:35:51,309
must be reduced to cinders!

1758
01:35:51,919 --> 01:35:55,029
Not a single soul
must be left alive.

1759
01:35:58,337 --> 01:35:59,869
Get ready for the final war!

1760
01:36:00,991 --> 01:36:02,991
[Music intensifies]

1761
01:36:09,264 --> 01:36:11,264
So it was with this wicked intent

1762
01:36:11,463 --> 01:36:13,939
that you granted the deeded land
in Kunnumpuram to strangers?

1763
01:36:14,058 --> 01:36:16,319
Davy, do not speak
such blasphemy!

1764
01:36:17,194 --> 01:36:20,099
How am I to know the true intentions
of those who come to purchase land?

1765
01:36:20,100 --> 01:36:21,100
Oh God!

1766
01:36:21,502 --> 01:36:23,694
Father, if what this boy has said
is true,

1767
01:36:23,695 --> 01:36:25,030
there is some deceit in it.

1768
01:36:25,031 --> 01:36:27,273
Oh! Accepting the pittance
those scoundrels gave you,

1769
01:36:27,274 --> 01:36:29,012
how could you betray us like this?

1770
01:36:29,013 --> 01:36:31,310
Devassy, I swear I didn't do
anything wrong on purpose.

1771
01:36:31,311 --> 01:36:32,498
I swear!

1772
01:36:32,801 --> 01:36:34,622
Will you all just stop it?

1773
01:36:35,936 --> 01:36:38,154
This isn't the time for you
to be fighting each other!

1774
01:36:40,000 --> 01:36:42,311
I had no clue where to go
or who to tell this to,

1775
01:36:42,312 --> 01:36:44,160
so I just took a
gamble and rushed here.

1776
01:36:44,161 --> 01:36:47,046
Unless you all unite,
put your minds to it and act,

1777
01:36:47,047 --> 01:36:48,484
they will set this land ablaze!

1778
01:36:48,485 --> 01:36:50,268
[Thunder rumbles]

1779
01:36:50,421 --> 01:36:52,107
- Father Cyriac!
- Yes?

1780
01:36:52,286 --> 01:36:54,599
Go quickly and book a trunk call
to the Bishop's House.

1781
01:36:54,600 --> 01:36:55,647
Okay.

1782
01:36:57,557 --> 01:36:58,637
Father,

1783
01:36:58,638 --> 01:37:00,578
there is complete turmoil
at Ayyathan Kovil too.

1784
01:37:00,871 --> 01:37:02,092
Arson… and cries for blood!

1785
01:37:02,303 --> 01:37:04,164
The people have been driven
out of their senses.

1786
01:37:04,165 --> 01:37:05,534
[Background music roars]

1787
01:37:06,544 --> 01:37:08,753
All my people are there.
May I go?

1788
01:37:10,570 --> 01:37:11,709
Son!

1789
01:37:14,558 --> 01:37:15,733
Thank you...

1790
01:37:16,047 --> 01:37:18,664
for coming all the way
at this hour to inform us.

1791
01:37:20,629 --> 01:37:21,911
Where are you from, my child?

1792
01:37:22,733 --> 01:37:23,895
From Puthuppally, Father.

1793
01:37:24,072 --> 01:37:25,108
What's your name?

1794
01:37:25,576 --> 01:37:26,640
MN Chandy!

1795
01:37:26,641 --> 01:37:29,674
[Earth-shaking background music]

1796
01:37:33,401 --> 01:37:35,503
Father! The phone's dead.

1797
01:37:35,899 --> 01:37:36,652
Oh no!

1798
01:37:36,653 --> 01:37:37,994
We have to go to the
police station, Father.

1799
01:37:37,995 --> 01:37:39,024
What for?

1800
01:37:39,025 --> 01:37:40,553
Which police do you trust now?

1801
01:37:40,809 --> 01:37:42,584
- Am I not right?
- Father...

1802
01:37:43,369 --> 01:37:44,690
What is happening, Father?

1803
01:37:45,698 --> 01:37:47,887
First, they said the Communists
were coming to kill us.

1804
01:37:48,365 --> 01:37:49,822
And now, the police!

1805
01:37:49,823 --> 01:37:51,503
What will we do now, Father?

1806
01:37:51,868 --> 01:37:54,024
Even the Lord Almighty
has forsaken us.

1807
01:37:54,359 --> 01:37:56,046
[Loud thunder]

1808
01:37:56,047 --> 01:37:57,047
Jesus!

1809
01:38:02,112 --> 01:38:04,112
[Fire crackling]

1810
01:38:05,323 --> 01:38:07,176
[Laughs loudly]

1811
01:38:10,362 --> 01:38:12,145
[Menacing laugh]

1812
01:38:13,602 --> 01:38:15,602
This is the land
where God is dead!

1813
01:38:15,945 --> 01:38:18,251
A land where there is
no one left to save us!

1814
01:38:18,504 --> 01:38:21,666
Run! Run!

1815
01:38:21,992 --> 01:38:24,704
If you want to live,
run for your lives!

1816
01:38:24,821 --> 01:38:25,828
Run away!

1817
01:38:26,132 --> 01:38:28,638
This land is about to go up in flames!

1818
01:38:29,491 --> 01:38:31,491
O Jehovah, God of Armies,

1819
01:38:32,171 --> 01:38:33,588
deliver us!

1820
01:38:34,362 --> 01:38:35,922
Shine Thy face upon us,

1821
01:38:36,554 --> 01:38:38,314
that we may be saved!

1822
01:38:39,271 --> 01:38:40,665
Manifest Thyself

1823
01:38:40,763 --> 01:38:42,314
for our sake!

1824
01:38:42,890 --> 01:38:44,890
[Thunder rumbles]

1825
01:38:48,159 --> 01:38:50,159
[Majestic background music rises]

1826
01:38:51,418 --> 01:38:52,425
[Church bell rings]

1827
01:39:00,057 --> 01:39:02,057
[Music intensifies]

1828
01:39:06,846 --> 01:39:08,913
Comrades, things are
spiralling out of control here.

1829
01:39:08,914 --> 01:39:11,148
Everyone is scared.
They've all gathered at the Church.

1830
01:39:11,247 --> 01:39:12,724
Word is, the police
are heading this way,

1831
01:39:12,725 --> 01:39:14,586
and they'll burn
Kunnumpuram to the ground.

1832
01:39:14,587 --> 01:39:16,180
We must do something!

1833
01:39:16,340 --> 01:39:18,340
[Boots approaching]

1834
01:39:19,234 --> 01:39:21,234
[Jeep approaches]

1835
01:39:28,062 --> 01:39:30,062
[Mournful music]

1836
01:39:37,827 --> 01:39:39,275
[Mournful background music rises]

1837
01:39:39,276 --> 01:39:41,496
[Crying]

1838
01:39:42,824 --> 01:39:44,824
[Music rises]

1839
01:39:47,982 --> 01:39:49,435
Thomapuram and Kaaniyaar

1840
01:39:50,169 --> 01:39:51,169
are not two,

1841
01:39:51,532 --> 01:39:53,155
but one.
That was my promise to her.

1842
01:39:56,863 --> 01:39:59,848
On this land, it wasn't a church
or a party office she wanted…

1843
01:40:00,431 --> 01:40:02,391
She wanted a school
to be built here…

1844
01:40:02,618 --> 01:40:04,572
And today, here she is...

1845
01:40:05,938 --> 01:40:06,938
Son...

1846
01:40:08,223 --> 01:40:09,384
Father,

1847
01:40:09,385 --> 01:40:10,665
I am not Pothan.

1848
01:40:10,917 --> 01:40:12,045
I am Krishna Pillai.

1849
01:40:16,233 --> 01:40:17,300
This is Joy.

1850
01:40:17,874 --> 01:40:18,961
He is a Dalit.

1851
01:40:20,516 --> 01:40:21,593
They are Communists.

1852
01:40:22,231 --> 01:40:23,537
These are Congressmen.

1853
01:40:24,139 --> 01:40:25,229
That one is a Nair…

1854
01:40:25,230 --> 01:40:26,269
This one is an Ezhava…

1855
01:40:26,270 --> 01:40:27,432
This one is an Adivasi.

1856
01:40:29,602 --> 01:40:32,635
Riots happen only in places where
people fail to see one another as human.

1857
01:40:33,192 --> 01:40:35,972
[Poignant music]

1858
01:40:37,206 --> 01:40:38,206
[Thunder]

1859
01:40:45,546 --> 01:40:47,092
We made a grave mistake, Christopher…

1860
01:40:47,347 --> 01:40:48,807
Some forty years ago...

1861
01:40:49,085 --> 01:40:51,085
when we migrated here
and settled on this land…

1862
01:40:51,747 --> 01:40:53,980
There were no divisions

1863
01:40:54,782 --> 01:40:56,403
of caste or religion among us.

1864
01:40:59,023 --> 01:41:00,500
For the sake of the Lord Almighty

1865
01:41:00,914 --> 01:41:03,137
grant us a chance
to redeem ourselves.

1866
01:41:04,114 --> 01:41:07,394
This is the land marked out

1867
01:41:08,344 --> 01:41:09,895
by those devils

1868
01:41:09,896 --> 01:41:12,160
for the greatest massacre
of the Liberation Struggle.

1869
01:41:12,689 --> 01:41:14,289
Before this night yields to dawn,

1870
01:41:15,004 --> 01:41:16,420
they will slaughter...

1871
01:41:16,872 --> 01:41:18,669
every one of these poor souls.

1872
01:41:18,840 --> 01:41:20,859
[Rain falling]

1873
01:41:20,860 --> 01:41:22,860
[Crying]

1874
01:41:24,223 --> 01:41:26,277
Brother, please don't leave us!

1875
01:41:27,344 --> 01:41:30,317
They are going to kill us.
I'm so scared!

1876
01:41:31,535 --> 01:41:32,723
[Emotional music]

1877
01:41:32,724 --> 01:41:33,744
This sight!

1878
01:41:34,078 --> 01:41:36,102
You must never, ever forget it!

1879
01:41:36,103 --> 01:41:37,329
This piercing wail...

1880
01:41:37,647 --> 01:41:39,647
must forever resonate
within your ears.

1881
01:41:40,670 --> 01:41:42,503
Once you have grown
into a man of mettle,

1882
01:41:42,929 --> 01:41:45,065
you must lead the fray to fight

1883
01:41:45,437 --> 01:41:47,091
for the righteous cause
of those who weep!

1884
01:41:55,355 --> 01:41:57,117
[Jeeps approaching]

1885
01:41:57,118 --> 01:41:58,118
[Kaaniyaar]

1886
01:42:00,590 --> 01:42:02,590
[Music swells]

1887
01:42:07,454 --> 01:42:09,454
[Music continues]

1888
01:42:14,711 --> 01:42:16,050
Which station are you from?

1889
01:42:16,473 --> 01:42:17,497
MSP.

1890
01:42:17,498 --> 01:42:18,649
Riot Police.

1891
01:42:19,279 --> 01:42:20,419
Understood?

1892
01:42:20,561 --> 01:42:22,563
[Ominous music]

1893
01:42:30,234 --> 01:42:32,234
[Music rises]

1894
01:42:32,595 --> 01:42:33,712
[Lighter flicks]

1895
01:42:38,146 --> 01:42:40,146
[Fire flares up]

1896
01:42:41,542 --> 01:42:43,262
[Crowd scatters in panic]

1897
01:42:43,450 --> 01:42:45,450
[Music intensifies]

1898
01:42:54,630 --> 01:42:56,630
[Music continues]

1899
01:42:56,921 --> 01:42:58,494
Batches K-1 and K-2 to the huts;

1900
01:42:58,624 --> 01:43:00,967
the rest, depart for
Kunnumpuram jetty and the grounds

1901
01:43:00,968 --> 01:43:02,025
at once.

1902
01:43:02,964 --> 01:43:04,611
Sir, the force is ready.

1903
01:43:09,663 --> 01:43:11,663
[Music continues]

1904
01:43:15,349 --> 01:43:17,225
Your time starts now!

1905
01:43:26,210 --> 01:43:28,323
[Intense music]

1906
01:43:31,691 --> 01:43:32,696
Move fast! Move fast!

1907
01:43:33,989 --> 01:43:35,389
Go, set the whole place ablaze!

1908
01:43:35,509 --> 01:43:37,015
Go! Go! Go! Go!

1909
01:43:38,535 --> 01:43:41,215
Everyone, move quickly!
Spare no one!

1910
01:43:42,369 --> 01:43:44,369
[Tense music]

1911
01:43:44,957 --> 01:43:46,675
- Come, come!
- I'm getting scared, mom.

1912
01:43:46,676 --> 01:43:47,822
Don't be scared, dear!

1913
01:43:49,935 --> 01:43:51,095
Leave me!

1914
01:43:52,439 --> 01:43:53,892
[Screams]

1915
01:43:54,967 --> 01:43:56,967
[Church bell rings]

1916
01:44:01,904 --> 01:44:03,222
[Church bell rings]

1917
01:44:03,931 --> 01:44:07,131
Where man and the devil
stand face to face,

1918
01:44:08,461 --> 01:44:10,235
what business does
God have there?

1919
01:44:10,236 --> 01:44:11,236
[Thunder]

1920
01:44:14,219 --> 01:44:15,339
[Music swells]

1921
01:44:22,785 --> 01:44:24,045
[Shouts]

1922
01:44:25,554 --> 01:44:28,033
[Heroic music]

1923
01:44:33,309 --> 01:44:35,309
[Music continues]

1924
01:44:41,629 --> 01:44:43,509
Christopher! Should we move them from here?

1925
01:44:44,837 --> 01:44:46,724
The slopes and ridges
of Kunnumpuram,

1926
01:44:47,055 --> 01:44:48,108
woods and hills,

1927
01:44:48,275 --> 01:44:49,445
are etched in our minds.

1928
01:44:50,674 --> 01:44:53,222
Even if the southern winds and
the monsoon rains come together,

1929
01:44:53,617 --> 01:44:54,984
the groves of Kunnumpuram,

1930
01:44:55,552 --> 01:44:57,185
are guarded by us,
with our very lives.

1931
01:44:57,995 --> 01:45:00,509
[Triumphant music]

1932
01:45:03,021 --> 01:45:04,197
You, head that way!

1933
01:45:12,328 --> 01:45:14,741
Christopher, we've got
nothing to fight with.

1934
01:45:14,934 --> 01:45:16,680
They're coming armed,
aren't they?

1935
01:45:18,829 --> 01:45:20,414
To confront them,
our weapon shall be…

1936
01:45:21,441 --> 01:45:22,460
this very land!

1937
01:45:23,116 --> 01:45:24,657
Weapons may fail us…

1938
01:45:24,805 --> 01:45:26,357
but this land never will!

1939
01:45:26,584 --> 01:45:28,004
[Majestic background music rises]

1940
01:45:29,071 --> 01:45:30,772
You there! Set it ablaze!

1941
01:45:40,059 --> 01:45:42,812
[Shouts]

1942
01:45:46,378 --> 01:45:47,766
Come face us, if you dare!

1943
01:45:48,620 --> 01:45:49,783
Bloody scum!

1944
01:45:50,909 --> 01:45:52,909
[Multiple people shouting]

1945
01:45:55,759 --> 01:45:57,759
[Shouting continues]

1946
01:46:02,450 --> 01:46:04,337
[Fierce battle]

1947
01:46:09,040 --> 01:46:11,040
[Battle cry]

1948
01:46:14,037 --> 01:46:16,037
[Heavy blows]

1949
01:46:17,405 --> 01:46:19,405
[Intense music]

1950
01:46:22,174 --> 01:46:23,807
Aashaan!

1951
01:46:35,229 --> 01:46:37,229
[Majestic background music rises]

1952
01:46:43,817 --> 01:46:45,817
[Shouts]

1953
01:46:48,837 --> 01:46:50,837
[Body hits the ground]

1954
01:47:01,187 --> 01:47:03,187
[Music continues]

1955
01:47:05,832 --> 01:47:07,584
This is the land
I was born into.

1956
01:47:08,220 --> 01:47:11,128
I will not let any filthy outsider
set foot here and seize power.

1957
01:47:12,457 --> 01:47:15,030
I'll gut him and throw him
into the river; no matter who he is!

1958
01:47:22,339 --> 01:47:24,285
[Music continues]

1959
01:47:31,022 --> 01:47:33,022
[Ferocious battle cry]

1960
01:47:35,779 --> 01:47:37,779
[Music rises]

1961
01:47:40,466 --> 01:47:41,466
[Battle cry]

1962
01:47:43,700 --> 01:47:44,810
Let go of me!

1963
01:47:45,807 --> 01:47:48,686
Aashaan, the police are heading
straight for our huts!

1964
01:47:48,687 --> 01:47:50,249
Don't let the police
get to the huts!

1965
01:47:53,095 --> 01:47:54,141
Quintal...

1966
01:47:57,750 --> 01:47:59,419
My boys and girls are in there!

1967
01:48:00,747 --> 01:48:02,747
[Battle cry]

1968
01:48:03,586 --> 01:48:04,844
To save our motherland,

1969
01:48:05,324 --> 01:48:06,637
we don't need miracles!

1970
01:48:08,701 --> 01:48:10,701
[Fierce battle cry]

1971
01:48:13,814 --> 01:48:16,108
It is enough that you remember
the moves and footwork

1972
01:48:16,109 --> 01:48:17,287
I taught you.

1973
01:48:19,348 --> 01:48:21,348
[Heavy blows]

1974
01:48:24,721 --> 01:48:25,721
Come on!

1975
01:48:26,794 --> 01:48:28,914
Didn't I tell you angels
would come to save us?

1976
01:48:30,269 --> 01:48:32,269
[Music rises]

1977
01:48:37,219 --> 01:48:38,713
[Music gradually fades]

1978
01:48:42,282 --> 01:48:43,782
Armed battalion K-3!

1979
01:48:44,553 --> 01:48:45,553
Charge!

1980
01:48:47,544 --> 01:48:49,544
[Music rises]

1981
01:48:54,933 --> 01:48:55,961
Go! Go! Go!

1982
01:49:04,182 --> 01:49:05,812
O Lord!
Is there no end to this?

1983
01:49:06,227 --> 01:49:08,525
Christopher,
more of them are coming!

1984
01:49:08,850 --> 01:49:09,923
They've got guns too!

1985
01:49:11,106 --> 01:49:13,046
Bring as many as you want.
Come on!

1986
01:49:14,254 --> 01:49:15,463
Look there!

1987
01:49:24,313 --> 01:49:26,313
[Arrow whooshes]

1988
01:49:28,558 --> 01:49:30,359
This river is your cradle!

1989
01:49:30,555 --> 01:49:32,068
Even with your eyes and feet bound,

1990
01:49:32,480 --> 01:49:35,105
you would cross the Amaravathi river,
unfazed by its whirlpools.

1991
01:49:35,454 --> 01:49:37,454
[Majestic music]

1992
01:49:39,724 --> 01:49:40,764
[Arrow whooshes]

1993
01:49:42,016 --> 01:49:43,600
That is the strength
we require today!

1994
01:49:43,865 --> 01:49:45,233
The history of the Kurumans

1995
01:49:45,234 --> 01:49:47,643
who buried the Kumbala army
in the waters of the Amaravathi,

1996
01:49:48,533 --> 01:49:49,936
must be repeated here
by you today!

1997
01:49:50,512 --> 01:49:52,512
[Music continues]

1998
01:49:55,625 --> 01:49:58,132
[Mysterious rumbling]

1999
01:49:59,057 --> 01:50:01,812
For He shall give His angels
charge over thee,

2000
01:50:01,813 --> 01:50:03,994
to keep thee in all thy ways.

2001
01:50:04,289 --> 01:50:06,289
[Rumbling continues]

2002
01:50:07,507 --> 01:50:09,507
[Splash]

2003
01:50:10,013 --> 01:50:12,274
They shall bear thee
up in their hands,

2004
01:50:12,475 --> 01:50:14,567
lest thou dash thy foot
against a stone.

2005
01:50:20,441 --> 01:50:23,587
The armies that defy thee
shall be scattered, and shall flee.

2006
01:50:25,041 --> 01:50:26,607
Master, it's all been poured.

2007
01:50:27,930 --> 01:50:28,984
[Whistles]

2008
01:50:30,227 --> 01:50:34,409
Thou shalt tread upon
the lion and the adder!

2009
01:50:37,673 --> 01:50:42,015
And thou shalt trample under foot
the lion and the serpent!

2010
01:50:42,016 --> 01:50:44,016
[Music rises]

2011
01:50:47,316 --> 01:50:48,347
[Fire spreading]

2012
01:50:48,348 --> 01:50:50,202
[Music rises]

2013
01:50:53,005 --> 01:50:55,005
[Music continues]

2014
01:50:57,477 --> 01:50:59,143
Bloody dog!

2015
01:51:12,285 --> 01:51:13,625
[Gunshot]

2016
01:51:15,871 --> 01:51:16,871
Huh!

2017
01:51:23,267 --> 01:51:24,401
Oh no!

2018
01:51:26,681 --> 01:51:27,681
[Screams]

2019
01:51:29,567 --> 01:51:31,340
Vareeth... Vareeth...

2020
01:51:31,341 --> 01:51:32,426
Vareeth...

2021
01:51:32,427 --> 01:51:33,427
[Gunshot]

2022
01:51:33,851 --> 01:51:35,001
Rathnakaran!

2023
01:51:47,605 --> 01:51:49,643
Rathnakaran!

2024
01:51:49,992 --> 01:51:50,997
Rathnakaran!

2025
01:51:53,047 --> 01:51:54,166
Vareeth!

2026
01:51:57,329 --> 01:51:58,609
Comrade!

2027
01:51:58,734 --> 01:51:59,934
[Ominous music]

2028
01:52:09,803 --> 01:52:11,803
[Music continues]

2029
01:52:24,576 --> 01:52:25,576
[Gunshot]

2030
01:52:28,259 --> 01:52:30,002
[Screams]

2031
01:52:31,574 --> 01:52:33,574
[Background music swells]

2032
01:52:50,204 --> 01:52:51,341
Trying to save them?

2033
01:52:53,252 --> 01:52:54,410
How many will you save?

2034
01:52:57,959 --> 01:52:59,560
Oh no! Christopher!

2035
01:52:59,923 --> 01:53:00,983
Christopher...!

2036
01:53:01,231 --> 01:53:02,779
Oh no! Blood!!

2037
01:53:03,445 --> 01:53:05,107
Kaaniyaar Kunnumpuram!

2038
01:53:05,499 --> 01:53:08,151
Do you think this land
is your father's property?

2039
01:53:10,408 --> 01:53:11,538
Christopher!

2040
01:53:12,428 --> 01:53:13,728
You come here and build huts,

2041
01:53:14,485 --> 01:53:15,758
you eat here,
you shit here…

2042
01:53:16,357 --> 01:53:18,011
And you think that makes
this land yours?

2043
01:53:21,559 --> 01:53:23,590
Christopher!
Oh no! Blood!

2044
01:53:23,591 --> 01:53:24,524
Christopher!!

2045
01:53:24,525 --> 01:53:28,391
This is deeded land, purchased
for the agreed price!

2046
01:53:33,869 --> 01:53:34,696
Christopher...

2047
01:53:34,795 --> 01:53:36,405
That defiant...

2048
01:53:37,056 --> 01:53:38,172
Ah!

2049
01:53:38,363 --> 01:53:39,436
That wretched actress!

2050
01:53:40,066 --> 01:53:41,952
I was me...

2051
01:53:42,346 --> 01:53:44,212
who shot her dead, point-blank.

2052
01:53:46,710 --> 01:53:48,891
A man got onto the bus alone,
with a gun in his hand.

2053
01:53:53,601 --> 01:53:54,601
Boom!

2054
01:53:56,870 --> 01:53:58,075
[Shouts]

2055
01:53:58,288 --> 01:53:59,346
Bloody...

2056
01:53:59,347 --> 01:54:01,347
[Powerful swing]

2057
01:54:03,260 --> 01:54:05,260
[Fierce combat]

2058
01:54:12,145 --> 01:54:14,145
[Music continues]

2059
01:54:46,495 --> 01:54:48,908
Kill them!
Bloody dogs!

2060
01:55:01,070 --> 01:55:02,237
Bloody!

2061
01:55:04,901 --> 01:55:06,016
Christopher!

2062
01:55:06,319 --> 01:55:08,074
Oh no! Christopher!

2063
01:55:08,511 --> 01:55:09,511
You!!

2064
01:55:10,074 --> 01:55:11,097
[Shouts]

2065
01:55:14,757 --> 01:55:17,005
Who the hell are you
to intervene, you dog?

2066
01:55:18,065 --> 01:55:19,358
[Blow lands]

2067
01:55:19,805 --> 01:55:21,805
[Intense music]

2068
01:55:27,115 --> 01:55:29,115
[Cry of pain]

2069
01:55:41,413 --> 01:55:42,829
Didn't you die yet?

2070
01:55:46,348 --> 01:55:47,414
Come on!

2071
01:55:48,940 --> 01:55:49,953
[Shouts]

2072
01:55:50,298 --> 01:55:51,298
Come!

2073
01:55:51,647 --> 01:55:53,668
[Battle cry]

2074
01:55:53,669 --> 01:55:54,935
Thrash him, Aashaan!

2075
01:56:08,977 --> 01:56:10,677
Beat them and drive them all out!

2076
01:56:11,833 --> 01:56:12,966
Out of the way!

2077
01:56:17,692 --> 01:56:19,692
[Shouts]

2078
01:56:29,878 --> 01:56:31,167
[Shouts]

2079
01:56:32,865 --> 01:56:34,476
[Music swells]

2080
01:57:01,214 --> 01:57:02,425
Whom are you doing this for?

2081
01:57:03,770 --> 01:57:05,770
[Laughs]

2082
01:57:07,322 --> 01:57:08,575
[Powerful strike]

2083
01:57:41,404 --> 01:57:44,379
The rightful lord
of this land will return…

2084
01:57:46,007 --> 01:57:47,180
To reclaim…

2085
01:57:47,325 --> 01:57:49,827
To reclaim this land!

2086
01:57:51,916 --> 01:57:55,011
Start digging your graves,
and await your end!

2087
01:57:55,365 --> 01:57:56,612
[Laughs loudly]

2088
01:57:59,240 --> 01:58:01,240
[Shouts loudly]

2089
01:58:03,289 --> 01:58:05,289
[Shouting continues]

2090
01:58:06,227 --> 01:58:08,227
[Music fades]

2091
01:58:15,699 --> 01:58:17,699
[Sobs]

2092
01:58:19,736 --> 01:58:21,736
[Gentle music]

2093
01:58:23,534 --> 01:58:26,360
[Breathing heavily]

2094
01:58:31,709 --> 01:58:33,841
You're all drenched, my child!

2095
01:58:44,408 --> 01:58:46,406
[Music continues]

2096
01:59:04,741 --> 01:59:06,337
[Painful groan]

2097
01:59:11,230 --> 01:59:12,230
[Crying]

2098
01:59:13,626 --> 01:59:14,897
I saw it!

2099
01:59:14,898 --> 01:59:15,861
What?

2100
01:59:15,862 --> 01:59:17,014
Seethamma!

2101
01:59:17,112 --> 01:59:19,160
When injustice fills the earth,

2102
01:59:19,754 --> 01:59:21,538
the Lord's messengers

2103
01:59:21,656 --> 01:59:23,104
shall guide our path.

2104
01:59:23,196 --> 01:59:24,622
[Music swells]

2105
01:59:26,896 --> 01:59:28,202
[Shouts]

2106
01:59:28,736 --> 01:59:30,429
The Almighty shall grant us

2107
01:59:31,503 --> 01:59:32,842
the strength we need.

2108
01:59:33,567 --> 01:59:36,647
[Background music rises]

2109
01:59:36,939 --> 01:59:38,172
He…

2110
01:59:38,793 --> 01:59:39,997
shall act through us…

2111
01:59:45,910 --> 01:59:47,842
to deliver His justice.

2112
01:59:48,249 --> 01:59:50,249
[Heroic music swells]

2113
02:00:14,368 --> 02:00:15,728
[Music continues]

2114
02:00:23,943 --> 02:00:25,242
[Music fades out]

2115
02:00:26,751 --> 02:00:29,351
[Church bell rings]

2116
02:00:30,641 --> 02:00:31,957
[Goat bleats]

2117
02:00:35,708 --> 02:00:40,161
The darkness that had long spread across
the skies of Kaaniyaar has now passed,

2118
02:00:41,409 --> 02:00:42,875
and light now
shines upon this land.

2119
02:00:44,829 --> 02:00:47,775
The heroes who have left us

2120
02:00:47,980 --> 02:00:49,980
shall forever remain
a part of history,

2121
02:00:50,468 --> 02:00:52,534
here, in Kaaniyaar.

2122
02:00:52,981 --> 02:00:54,981
[Crying]

2123
02:00:55,123 --> 02:00:57,123
[Mournful music]

2124
02:01:08,176 --> 02:01:09,493
Along with them,

2125
02:01:09,494 --> 02:01:12,527
an angel who cherished a noble dream
also departed from us.

2126
02:01:13,122 --> 02:01:15,122
[Music swells]

2127
02:01:18,547 --> 02:01:20,360
No matter how far I may go…

2128
02:01:21,495 --> 02:01:22,869
when I close my eyes,

2129
02:01:23,374 --> 02:01:25,061
the very first image
that comes to me…

2130
02:01:25,393 --> 02:01:27,393
is this river… and this land.

2131
02:01:32,436 --> 02:01:33,895
Here on our Kurishumala,

2132
02:01:34,086 --> 02:01:35,552
just as she had envisioned,

2133
02:01:37,157 --> 02:01:39,157
beyond all barriers
of caste and creed,

2134
02:01:39,556 --> 02:01:42,404
for every child of this land,

2135
02:01:42,405 --> 02:01:44,281
we shall establish a school.

2136
02:01:47,180 --> 02:01:50,434
The one who helped us
reclaim our land…

2137
02:01:50,556 --> 02:01:51,569
It was him!

2138
02:01:53,161 --> 02:01:56,137
To safeguard our church
and our land,

2139
02:01:56,364 --> 02:01:58,030
to lead us on the righteous path…

2140
02:01:58,258 --> 02:02:00,614
the one whom the Lord Almighty
christened and sent unto us,

2141
02:02:01,743 --> 02:02:03,314
our…

2142
02:02:03,588 --> 02:02:04,877
our Christopher!

2143
02:02:07,432 --> 02:02:08,854
Our Krishna Pillai!

2144
02:02:12,492 --> 02:02:14,667
Our own Church Rowdy!

2145
02:02:14,844 --> 02:02:16,844
[Music intensifies]

2146
02:02:19,752 --> 02:02:21,421
In pursuit of God's land,

2147
02:02:21,886 --> 02:02:23,592
more devils shall emerge.

2148
02:02:26,252 --> 02:02:27,425
Even then…

2149
02:02:27,646 --> 02:02:29,432
as the protector of this land…

2150
02:02:30,058 --> 02:02:31,391
he shall remain here.

2151
02:02:32,030 --> 02:02:33,292
with us.

2152
02:02:39,450 --> 02:02:42,425
The rightful lord
of this land will return…

2153
02:02:43,439 --> 02:02:44,476
To reclaim…

2154
02:02:44,477 --> 02:02:47,012
To reclaim this land!

2155
02:02:49,021 --> 02:02:52,116
Start digging your graves,
and await your end!

2156
02:02:53,933 --> 02:02:56,613
It was not I

2157
02:02:57,188 --> 02:02:58,608
who sent him

2158
02:02:58,967 --> 02:02:59,967
to the land of Kaaniyaar.

2159
02:03:02,112 --> 02:03:04,687
No matter how many years may pass,

2160
02:03:05,317 --> 02:03:08,843
he shall certainly find the devil

2161
02:03:09,414 --> 02:03:12,016
who waits to claim that land.

2162
02:03:13,920 --> 02:03:15,003
That...

2163
02:03:15,004 --> 02:03:16,135
[Laughs]

2164
02:03:16,136 --> 02:03:18,053
is divine decree.

2165
02:03:18,054 --> 02:03:20,684
[After many years in Thalakkaveri...]

2166
02:03:21,669 --> 02:03:23,601
[Festive music]

2167
02:03:29,261 --> 02:03:30,751
[Explosion]

2168
02:03:36,177 --> 02:03:38,177
[Music intensifies]

2169
02:03:39,196 --> 02:03:44,219
Not without reason did
the forests of Chandragiri

2170
02:03:44,951 --> 02:03:46,339
spare him, and him alone…

2171
02:03:46,448 --> 02:03:47,728
[Krishna Pillai]

2172
02:03:50,084 --> 02:03:53,092
[Powerful background music rises]

2173
02:04:25,264 --> 02:04:26,264
[Pillai...]

2174
02:04:26,788 --> 02:04:28,229
[Kelu Pappa]

2175
02:04:30,656 --> 02:04:31,696
[Gunshot]

2176
02:04:32,141 --> 02:04:37,414
For every soul that perished on this soil,
unavenged and denied of justice...

2177
02:04:37,987 --> 02:04:40,833
God shall wage His war...
with him as the weapon.

2178
02:04:42,568 --> 02:04:44,748
[Laughs]

2179
02:04:46,280 --> 02:04:47,674
[Blade pierces flesh]

2180
02:04:48,046 --> 02:04:49,646
[Heroic music rises]

2181
02:04:53,806 --> 02:04:55,345
[Horse neighs]

2182
02:04:57,435 --> 02:04:59,435
[Background music intensifies]

2183
02:05:06,953 --> 02:05:09,043
On this land, for all
that sprouts and grows,

2184
02:05:09,044 --> 02:05:11,746
and all that dies and decays,
there is only one sovereign!

2185
02:05:13,530 --> 02:05:14,530
Me!

2186
02:05:14,694 --> 02:05:15,767
[Bone cracks]

2187
02:05:16,614 --> 02:05:18,244
Pattelar Kunjambu Nambiar!

2188
02:05:25,919 --> 02:05:27,919
[Music intensifies]

2189
02:05:37,995 --> 02:05:39,995
[Blade whooshes]

2190
02:05:46,012 --> 02:05:47,905
[Blade whooshes]

2191
02:05:49,705 --> 02:05:51,192
[Bodies hit the ground]

2192
02:05:52,028 --> 02:05:56,259
Which low-bred wretch thinks
he has the right to speak my name?

2193
02:05:58,028 --> 02:05:59,726
Have you come to settle the score

2194
02:05:59,727 --> 02:06:02,675
for your old man, that hag,
and the rat-hole I burned to ash?

2195
02:06:05,191 --> 02:06:06,191
Or...

2196
02:06:06,369 --> 02:06:08,369
[Intense music rises]

2197
02:06:09,726 --> 02:06:10,782
[Knife thrown]

2198
02:06:14,330 --> 02:06:16,330
[Intense music]

2199
02:06:19,921 --> 02:06:21,060
Come!

2200
02:06:21,341 --> 02:06:23,341
[Music swells]

2201
02:06:27,859 --> 02:06:29,405
Come, let's begin.

2202
02:06:32,995 --> 02:06:35,034
[Music reaches its peak]

2203
02:06:35,035 --> 02:06:37,035
[Loud shout]

2204
02:06:37,438 --> 02:06:39,438
[Weapon whooshes]

2205
02:06:40,372 --> 02:06:41,565
[Gunshot]

2206
02:06:49,940 --> 02:06:52,417
[Background music continues]

